{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really","id":1342413,"title":"Why did gangrels leave the Camarilla ? I mean, really ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-19T14:56:53-07:00","id":1342413,"title":"Why did gangrels leave the Camarilla ? I mean, really ?","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> There's a lot of things I don't understand about the reason(s) why the gangrels leaved the Camarilla. I assume I don't have all the right informations.<br /> With the few things I know about this, the situations sounds like this :<br /> <b>Xaviar :</b> &quot;I met a really strange and god-like powerful thing ! It surely was a mathuselah !&quot;<br /> <b>Camarilla :</b> &quot;Lol. Mathuselahs don't exist.&quot;<br /> <b>Xaviar :</b> &quot;Alright then ! I am sure about this, and you hypocrites made me risk my life on it ! Me and my fellows leave this hypocrital organisation !&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's it. I want to make my players live this separation, and I have many questions about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Why shouldn't the Camarilla believe in mathusela's existence ?</b></i> I mean, they are myths, but vampires are myths. Why old vampires with god-like powers should be this unthinkable ? Do they lie about it ? If they do, why ?<br /> <br /> I can understand why Xaviar is bored with Camarilla. <i><b>But why all the clan leaved it ?</b></i> I really don't get that.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your lights, kindreds !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24796-honeyarty","name":"HoneyArty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T15:08:09-07:00","id":1342415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HoneyArty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really#post1342413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> There's a lot of things I don't understand about the reason(s) why the gangrels leaved the Camarilla. I assume I don't have all the right informations.<br /> With the few things I know about this, the situations sounds like this :<br /> <b>Xaviar :</b> &quot;I met a really strange and god-like powerful thing ! It surely was a mathuselah !&quot;<br /> <b>Camarilla :</b> &quot;Lol. Mathuselahs don't exist.&quot;<br /> <b>Xaviar :</b> &quot;Alright then ! I am sure about this, and you hypocrites made me risk my life on it ! Me and my fellows leave this hypocrital organisation !&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's it. I want to make my players live this separation, and I have many questions about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Why shouldn't the Camarilla believe in mathusela's existence ?</b></i> I mean, they are myths, but vampires are myths. Why old vampires with god-like powers should be this unthinkable ? Do they lie about it ? If they do, why ?<br /> <br /> I can understand why Xaviar is bored with Camarilla. <i><b>But why all the clan leaved it ?</b></i> I really don't get that.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your lights, kindreds !</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is this:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gangrel are cannon fodder. That's the way the Camarilla used them and the way the Camarilla considered them. The Camarilla were upset by Xavier talking about Antediluvians and the apocalypse when they wanted the Gangrel to go kill Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla denies the existence of the Antediluvians in order to justify its power. As long as the 3rd generation is a myth, even if the Inner Council KNOW its a lie (remember they met to talk about Cappadochias) then they can present themselves as the supreme authority of vampiredom. The Camarilla acknowledges old as fuck vampires exist but the Clan Founders? No.<br /> <br /> 3. Faced with horrifying godlike power and the possible dawn of Gehenna while the Camarilla was worried about a few Sabbat war parties as well as the recognition the Gangrel were nothing more than toy soldiers on a map, Xavier took the Gangrel from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> What did they lose, really?<br /> <br /> Membership on the Inner Council? As if most Gangrel benefited from that. A Justicar? Xavier was there for them anyway. Archons and Sheriffs? They stayed loyal for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T15:37:27-07:00","id":1342418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HoneyArty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really#post1342413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Why shouldn't the Camarilla believe in mathusela's existence ?</b></i> I mean, they are myths, but vampires are myths. Why old vampires with god-like powers should be this unthinkable ? Do they lie about it ? If they do, why ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Methuselahs are vampires who are over 1,000 years old, any vampire can become one after enough time has passed. Antedeluvians are the ones the Camarilla denies the existence of. They're the ones who created the clans, and have been around since before the biblical flood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:00:44-07:00","id":1342420,"title":"","content":"On Monday, 26 July 1999, Xaviar addressed a Gangrel Gather in Clinton County, New York to fight a &quot;Toreador&quot; who had fleshcrafting abilities. All the Gangrel fought this neonate named Leopold in Adirondack State Park, but he had the Eye of Hazimel (artifact that allowed him to use Chimerstry 9) and was used mostly as a catalyst for the Eldest's (Tzimisce Antediluvian resting beneath New York) powers of Vicissitude and Koldunic Sorcery. This decimated the Gangrel with very few survivors.<br /> <br /> In truth, Leopold, who himself believed to be the childe of Victoria Ash, was Gary Pennington, a Tremere antitribu, childe of Nickolai (who orchestrated the death of Petrodon), but he was heavily dominated and didn't know that himself.<br /> <br /> Xaviar went to the Camarilla council that was dealing with the Sabbat attack on the US East Coast and wanted to gather everyone in the Camarilla and fight this &quot;antediluvian&quot;, but they scoffed at his demands. In anger, he left and took everyone who was follow him. He went from city to city to speak with Gangrel of note to follow him out of the sect. Many agreed, a few notable stayed like Karsh.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:40:19-07:00","id":1342433,"title":"","content":"It's another sign Jan Pieterszoon is shit at his job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T17:08:58-07:00","id":1342437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342433#post1342433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's another sign Jan Pieterszoon is shit at his job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *was<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T20:48:22-07:00","id":1342455,"title":"","content":"The entire event was utterly contrived in order for the game to have an &quot;event&quot;. For that to happen, there were several things that had to happen, and any number of which lead to various points of disagreement by players. So if you don't get it, you're not alone. It was just one of many, many bad decisions during the Revised metaplot era. Every gaming group I personally know of has just ignored it.<br /> <br /> But if it's to your taste, then enjoy. But I'd recommend changing the event in order for its conclusion to make sense to you and your gaming group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T21:01:40-07:00","id":1342459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342455#post1342455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire event was utterly contrived in order for the game to have an &quot;event&quot;. For that to happen, there were several things that had to happen, and any number of which lead to various points of disagreement by players. So if you don't get it, you're not alone. It was just one of many, many bad decisions during the Revised metaplot era. Every gaming group I personally know of has just ignored it.<br /> <br /> But if it's to your taste, then enjoy. But I'd recommend changing the event in order for its conclusion to make sense to you and your gaming group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it as a set up for the Brujah and Gangrel to form their own Camarilla with blackjack, hookers, and Setites.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T21:47:51-07:00","id":1342463,"title":"","content":"Canonically, Xavier thought he met an Antediluvian. He didn't, actually, but this was sufficient impetus for all Gangrel to leave the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> This is, imo, kind of unsatisfying, and doesn't make a lot of sense: sure Xavier is a cool guy, but that many Gangrel abandoning their sect because he thought he saw a spooky thing?<br /> <br /> So I tend to run it differently. <i>What follows is <b>not canon</b> unless you decide you want it to be at your table, but it's what makes the most sense to me. It's also told from a very definitely Anarch perspective, since when this story came up in game, it was being used as a recruitment tool by an Anarch.</i> But I'm a big fan of unreliable narrators and multiple versions of every story, so here goes:<br /> <br /> See, the Camarilla had never really <i>liked</i> the Gangrel. You don't need wolves and savage beasts in your ivory tower. They made great guards and soldiers, especially with Protean's combat potential, but they were always a Low Clan and treated as inferior by the &quot;blue-blooded&quot; Ventrue and &quot;refined&quot; Torries. They stuck around mostly for the protections the Cam offered, because it was better to have a safety net than to be entirely alone.<br /> <br /> When Xavier went from city to city calling for his clanmates to join him, the influential bit wasn't &quot;I met an Antediluvian and Hardestadt doesn't believe me&quot;\u2014it was &quot;look, the Camarilla just sent hundreds of Gangrel to their Final Deaths to protect their own interests; if you abandon the Cam and join me, you won't be going off on your own, you'll have your whole clan watching your back, and that's more than the Camarilla will ever offer you&quot;. And that was pretty tempting compared to what the Cam was apparently selling (&quot;we might sometimes pretend not to think you're inferior\u2026to your face at least\u2026as long as you do everything we say and lay down your unlife on command to protect us&quot;).<br /> <br /> But that\u2026really doesn't look great for the Cam. The Gangrel aren't the only Low Clan who's gotten the short end of the protection deal. If the Gangrel left, what stops the Brujah from doing the same? And the Nos? And the Malks? The whole Ivory Tower system is great for the 1% at the top, but can't function without a 99% who are willing to spend their unlives supporting that 1%. So they spun the story differently. Instead of &quot;we mistreated the Gangrel until they finally had enough of it and fought back&quot;, it became &quot;this one delusional Gangrel thought he met an Antediluvian\u2014he didn't, btw\u2014and when we asked him to present any shred of evidence to support this, he went off to go be feral in the woods or something instead&quot;. That's the version most Camarilla neonates have heard, and the Elders are banking on them never looking at it closely enough to notice that the details don't line up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 10-20-2019, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T22:16:57-07:00","id":1342469,"title":"","content":"I use the Sabbat War for something similar, actually.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel were basically informed they were to be the front line soldiers of the Camarilla with the Brujah and were expected to fight as well as die for the Ventrue, Toreador, as well as Tremere that were sitting behind. That immediately rubbed a lot of them the wrong way as the Camarilla is not an organization that inspires LOYALTY. It inspires greed and it might inspire security but who, exactly, is loyal to an organization that exists solely to protect people who aren't you?<br /> <br /> Jan screwed up royally because he never even considered inviting them to the table.<br /> <br /> They were like furniture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T04:04:05-07:00","id":1342498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342415#post1342415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla denies the existence of the Antediluvians in order to justify its power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wich itself was a mistery for me considering:<br /> <b>Tremere:</b> the whole existence of the Clan was &quot;justified&quot; by Tremere consuming Saulot, the well known Antediluvian of the Salubri, and Tremere himself became one<br /> <b>Brujah:</b> Trolie is not really a myth of the Clan nor Carthage<br /> <b>Nosferatu</b>: built around a fear so strong of their Antediluvian and Absimiliard's children, they happily set aside and Antitribu/main clan arguments , designed the ShrekNet to monitor Nictuku movement and their Warens are basically fortified ... forts to defend themselves from the said ancient monsters<br /> <b>Gangrel: </b>They, like the Ventrue proudly tell you their linaege back to Ennoia, who was a regular on the Grand Gangrel Gatherings<br /> <b>Toreador</b> and <b>Ventrue</b>: both a clan proudly list her linaege bact to the Antediluvian, base of the Ventrue power is that theri antediluvian was apointed Caine himself to rule over the others, while the Toreador had their Antediluvan chilin around with them, not to mention they are porud to have/had Michael in their rank<br /> <b>Malkav:</b> Okay, nobody cares about them, but they ARE their Antediluvian... but okay, they are mostly ignored","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T04:42:14-07:00","id":1342499,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel joining the Camarilla despite it being antithetical to their very core identity, and the Camarilla disbelieving in the existence of the Antediluvians because Hardestadt the Fuckwit said so, strike me as having the very same problem:<br /> <br /> <b>Old White-Wolf had a policy of &quot;create first, ham-fist rationale later&quot; when it came to the first two editions.</b><br /> <br /> I never got the Gangrel ever joining the Camarilla in the first place. Almost entirely apolitical, like living like survivalists or hunters or just straight-up feral animals, hate being treated like they exist purely for the pleasure and vanity of the Toreador and Ventrue, and absolutely despise the Tremere over so many of them being made into Gargoyles? <i>Of course</i> they'd join the Camarilla... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also never got the Antediluvian-disbelief of the Camarilla. Unless your entire membership is comprised of 1% gods and 99% drooling halfwits who have precisely zero intelligent and deductive reasoning, the whole thing falls apart as soon as your Clan starts talking about their Antediluvian and folks start questioning how there's supposedly no such thing as the third generation.<br /> <br /> Its almost as contrary to logic as the Sabbat - who are supposedly dedicated to saving all of Kindred kind from the Antediluvians - having as its core Clans the two who (a) already took care of their own Antediluvians and (b) are easily so twisted that its impossible to imagine them not going so far as to line up to feed the members of other Clans to their Antediluvians if it would eliminate the competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:39:52-07:00","id":1342512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342498#post1342498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wich itself was a mistery for me considering:<br /> <b>Tremere:</b> the whole existence of the Clan was &quot;justified&quot; by Tremere consuming Saulot, the well known Antediluvian of the Salubri, and Tremere himself became one<br /> <b>Brujah:</b> Trolie is not really a myth of the Clan nor Carthage<br /> <b>Nosferatu</b>: built around a fear so strong of their Antediluvian and Absimiliard's children, they happily set aside and Antitribu/main clan arguments , designed the ShrekNet to monitor Nictuku movement and their Warens are basically fortified ... forts to defend themselves from the said ancient monsters<br /> <b>Gangrel: </b>They, like the Ventrue proudly tell you their linaege back to Ennoia, who was a regular on the Grand Gangrel Gatherings<br /> <b>Toreador</b> and <b>Ventrue</b>: both a clan proudly list her linaege bact to the Antediluvian, base of the Ventrue power is that theri antediluvian was apointed Caine himself to rule over the others, while the Toreador had their Antediluvan chilin around with them, not to mention they are porud to have/had Michael in their rank<br /> <b>Malkav:</b> Okay, nobody cares about them, but they ARE their Antediluvian... but okay, they are mostly ignored</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">That is very true, which is why many of the upper echelons of the Camarialla know, or suspect that the story is true. But they also know that rumors are rumors, and Vampires are deceitful and may be lying as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Then there is the other factor for saying that the antediluvians do not exist. To control the young. To admit their existence is to also to admit the Book of Nod may be true and therefore the Sabbat may be right Gehenna may come and so on. So the Camarilla has very good reasons for denying the Antediluvians existence and to declare the book of Nod as Heresy.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T07:07:51-07:00","id":1342519,"title":"","content":"I think, we as players/readers have too much knowledge of &quot;facts&quot; surrounding the game. It was always heavily implied (down to the Gehenna book) that &quot;all the myths are real&quot;. That was compounded by the fact that a lot of ancient power players (aka Methuselahs) were still active in the setting, thus theoretically having witnessed events first hand. That was one of the things that Requiem tried to turn into unreliable narration through the &quot;fog of ages&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Masquerade never made the attempt to remove knowledge from the game. Quite the opposite, with games lines such a Dark Ages, and chronicles like the Giovanni Chronicles, the myths surrounding the Tremere and Giovanni were verified.<br /> <br /> Even Carthage isn't much of a myth. Except that the presence of Baali puts a different spin on this supposed &quot;utopia&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is one thing to use myths and legends as a validation of power (Gangrel, Toreador, Ventrue, Nosferatu), but another thing to be confronted that those validations do actually exist.<br /> <br /> Consider the in-game angle: Lineage back to a mythical antediluvian is a justification for the right to rule. Boasting that one's antediluvian sat at the Gathers also paints a certain picture of the clan. Using unseen monsters to keep your childer in line is also a valid reason to tell a myth (fear the monster that is more monstrous than us), lastly Carthage is big propaganda for the Brujah to rally around. No matter if it is true or not.<br /> <br /> The &quot;failing&quot; of the older Vampire material was to treat this myths as real and true, thereby dispelling their mythological nature and getting the players to accept them as real, because the sourcebooks backed them up.<br /> <br /> Now, we are left today with the conundrum to turn accepted truths of the setting back into the myths they should be. That makes it hard to wrap our heads around certain events in the setting.<br /> <br /> Compared with an average Neonate on the streets, we are Noddist scholars on par with Vykos and Beckett. Just to put things into perspective. We as readers have a library of Noddist lore to draw on that would take them centuries to gather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T07:11:38-07:00","id":1342520,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel joined the Camarilla because it was a way of keeping everyone out of their business. Then the Camarilla got in their business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T07:26:47-07:00","id":1342526,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel were in the Camarilla at the launch of the game's first edition because the Camarilla was treated as the only playable faction at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T08:24:28-07:00","id":1342532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342526#post1342526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel were in the Camarilla at the launch of the game's first edition because the Camarilla was treated as the only playable faction at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This<br /> They wanted playable versions of every major vampire archetype, from the ratlike Nosferatu, to the hypnotic aristocratic Bela Lugosi, to the beautiful Anne Rice vamps, to the feral Near Dark vampires. Gangrel were created, basically, so you could play vampires with the classic ability to turn into bats and wolves. And they were Camarilla because that's all there was initially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T11:18:31-07:00","id":1342556,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Camarilla\u2019s official position was that the Antediluvians were all destroyed during the Great Flood. I mean, if they never existed, then where did the clans come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T12:33:55-07:00","id":1342563,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's less &quot;the Antediluvians never existed&quot; and more &quot;they're all dead, we don't need to worry about them any more&quot;. Why pay any attention to [Ventrue], who is gone, when Hardestadt is still alive and right here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T13:16:50-07:00","id":1342567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342556#post1342556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Camarilla\u2019s official position was that the Antediluvians were all destroyed during the Great Flood. I mean, if they never existed, then where did the clans come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its just a myth. Vampires evolved or whatever you &quot;scientists&quot; believe now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342526#post1342526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel were in the Camarilla at the launch of the game's first edition because the Camarilla was treated as the only playable faction at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why the Gangrel wouldn't join up. The only problem is when the Camarilla started asking more than they gave. Gangrel aren't anti-social, they're just less social than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T13:38:11-07:00","id":1342568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342556#post1342556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Camarilla\u2019s official position was that the Antediluvians were all destroyed during the Great Flood. I mean, if they never existed, then where did the clans come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth keeping in mind that the term &quot;Antediluvian&quot; carries a lot of in-setting baggage; ancient, all powerful blood gods who engage in a massive millennia long war with one another and who will rise up to devour their progeny. Between things like the Book of Nod, stories of Enoch and Caine, the Sabbat, etc, there are certain concepts that tend to be intrinsic to the Antediluvian and I believe those concepts are more what the Camarilla denies.<br /> <br /> When the Camarilla says that, &quot;the Antediluvians don't exist&quot; I believe it's more that the Antediluvians you hear about as ancient blood gods who are going to destroy the world don't exist. The Clans have founders of course, but those founders were just like, vampires, you know? Powerful ones sure, but not legendary or mythical ones and definitely not vampires that pose an existential threat to the world. They're mostly dead and even if they're not and one of them woke up, they'd be more confused about the modern world than any kind of danger to vampires as a whole.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that members of the Inner Council did meet Antediluvians such as Cappadocius. And keep in mind what happened to him. He was basically a bumblefuck who got himself diablarized and his Clan ended up in the dustbin of history. <i>The End.</i> Omniscient, all powerful blood god he certainly was not. If other Clan Founders were as comically incompetent as he was (and considering most of them are widely believed to be dead or diablarized it wouldn't exactly be wrong to think that about them) then there's really no reason to be so freaked out over them waking up.<br /> <br /> The awakening of Ravnos obviously changes that up quite a bit because suddenly Antediluvian as ancient, (nearly) all powerful blood god who rises up to devour their progeny turns out to be true, or at least close enough that it's worth reassessing the ideas about Clan founders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-20-2019, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T13:40:57-07:00","id":1342570,"title":"","content":"When you have a logic issue remember that emotion and mind control are ever present in this genre. <br /> <br /> Even real world fanaticism may seem illogical to you but know that it is what it is. <br /> <br /> You can justify any, all, or none to match your table\u2019s plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T13:58:36-07:00","id":1342574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342568#post1342568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth remembering that members of the Inner Council did meet Antediluvians such as Cappadocius. And keep in mind what happened to him. He was basically a bumblefuck who got himself diablarized and his Clan ended up in the dustbin of history. <i>The End.</i> Omniscient, all powerful blood god he certainly was not. If other Clan Founders were as comically incompetent as he was (and considering most of them are widely believed to be dead or diablarized it wouldn't exactly be wrong to think that about them) then there's really no reason to be so freaked out over them waking up.<br /> <br /> The awakening of Ravnos obviously changes that up quite a bit because suddenly Antediluvian as ancient, (nearly) all powerful blood god who rises up to devour their progeny turns out to be true, or at least close enough that it's worth reassessing the ideas about Clan founders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this assumes the Camarilla isn't the kind of people who wouldn't bald face lie to the majority of vampiredom about water being wet.<br /> <br /> They're awful people and don't care about the truth.<br /> <br /> Why should they?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T14:05:21-07:00","id":1342578,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> I totally agree with you.<br /> <br /> But didn\u2019t the whole Ravnos thing get retconned by V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T14:18:55-07:00","id":1342579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342578#post1342578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But didn\u2019t the whole Ravnos thing get retconned by V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's gotten retconned and un-retconned a few times. The Week of Nightmares loresheet implies it's currently un-retconned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T14:25:12-07:00","id":1342580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342556#post1342556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Camarilla\u2019s official position was that the Antediluvians were all destroyed during the Great Flood. I mean, if they never existed, then where did the clans come from?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it's kinda a hypocrite point of view imposed by the elders that know their genealogy up to Caine.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T15:51:10-07:00","id":1342589,"title":"","content":"A few points.<br /> <br /> First, as Reasor said, the Camarilla weren't just a sect in first edition, they were THE vampire government/society. Any given vampire was assumed to be Camarilla by default, or else a rebellious Anarch (which in first edition was synonymous with &quot;Neonate&quot;). Later editions would pivot to saying that the Camarilla <i>declares</i> all Kindred to be under their purview; that's their party line. The Sabbat in those early days were a mysterious, probably satanic doomsday cult that operated as scattered cells (packs). It's only later that they were expanded, and deepened, and organized, and broken up into dozens of factions and political stances and hierarchies.<br /> <br /> Point being, it's not so strange the Gangrel were made Camarilla. What the Camarilla even WAS took a while to solidify, and was subject to drift.<br /> <br /> Second, and related to the first, because the Sabbat was considered a doomsday cult, it's assumed that their entire ethos - Noddism included - is mysterious to most non-Sabbat Kindred. WE, as players/storytellers, know all about the mytho-history of VtM. The people living IN IT, meanwhile, cannot be assumed to. Vampires operate under an all-encompassing veil of secrecy, both to conceal themselves from mortals AND to keep a given vampire group's operations and secrets hidden from <i>other vampires</i>. Even what Kindred think they &quot;know&quot; should be shrouded in multiple layers of disinformation, in-group biases against out-groups, and a healthy amount of cultural assumptions informed by over a century of mass media depictions of vampires.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, I wish the &quot;Kindred Lore&quot; ability were more prominent as a tool for determining, mechanically, how much a character knows about their splat.)<br /> <br /> Third, the Camarilla's &quot;public&quot; stance is less &quot;the Antedeluvians don't exist&quot;, and more &quot;the Antedeluvians are not RELEVANT&quot;. The Ivory Tower maintains its power by every other vampire in their domains bending the knee to the ones in charge. They have a vested interest in suppressing any knowledge of Noddism. Both because it's the theology espoused by the Sabbat, who are the Camarilla's greatest enemies, and because if no one knows who founded the Clans and what they were about, the Camarilla can make up whatever &quot;history&quot; is most convenient. Why do you think Archons and Alastors spend so much time hunting down Noddist &quot;heresies&quot;? Young vampires who hear about Noddist teachings - who start to believe in horrific blood gods from antiquity - will stop listening to their elders in the Camarilla, and start listening to the Sabbat recruiters who preach about an end-of-nights to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:10:31-07:00","id":1342594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342563#post1342563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's less &quot;the Antediluvians never existed&quot; and more &quot;they're all dead, we don't need to worry about them any more&quot;. Why pay any attention to [Ventrue], who is gone, when Hardestadt is still alive and right here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, because we all know how easily vampires can drown, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:10:43-07:00","id":1342595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342589#post1342589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, the Camarilla's &quot;public&quot; stance is less &quot;the Antedeluvians don't exist&quot;, and more &quot;the Antedeluvians are not RELEVANT&quot;. The Ivory Tower maintains its power by every other vampire in their domains bending the knee to the ones in charge. They have a vested interest in suppressing any knowledge of Noddism. Both because it's the theology espoused by the Sabbat, who are the Camarilla's greatest enemies, and because if no one knows who founded the Clans and what they were about, the Camarilla can make up whatever &quot;history&quot; is most convenient. Why do you think Archons and Alastors spend so much time hunting down Noddist &quot;heresies&quot;? Young vampires who hear about Noddist teachings - who start to believe in horrific blood gods from antiquity - will stop listening to their elders in the Camarilla, and start listening to the Sabbat recruiters who preach about an end-of-nights to come.</div> </div> </div> </div>Over time, the <b>Book of Nod </b>went from a commonly owned book of Kindred mythology to contraband that will get you killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:15:05-07:00","id":1342597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342574#post1342574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this assumes the Camarilla isn't the kind of people who wouldn't bald face lie to the majority of vampiredom about water being wet.<br /> <br /> They're awful people and don't care about the truth.<br /> <br /> Why should they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think they absolutely would give a bald face lie to vampires, if they had something to get out of it. In this case, I'm not sure they would?<br /> <br /> I mean, what would they have to get out of saying, &quot;There are no antediluvians, there are no Clan founders, the Clans just sprung up, fully formed like Athena sprung forth from the mind of Zeus,&quot; rather than, &quot;Yeah, there were presumably Clan founders. They weren't blood gods, they weren't mythical antediluvians, honestly, they weren't shit. They were just vampires, quite a few of them have been killed and the rest are gone or asleep. <i>If</i> any show up, they'll also get killed, so why worry about them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, my interpretation is a bit colored by the various Clanbooks. Those books tend to be written from an in-character perspective, and represent a sort of generic &quot;here's how things work&quot; primer that would be a reasonable example for player characters have received. And when it comes to the Camarilla clans, those also mention Clan founders and antediluvians.<br /> <br /> So it's always seemed to me that in-setting, if the Camarilla's argument was that there are no Clan founders, nobody believes that for a second which would leave the Camarilla just looking like obvious dummies for trying to insist that the Clans don't have founders. Which is why I tend to believe they don't try to push that and instead just push the idea that Clan founders weren't particularly powerful, they weren't boogymen and that if any of them do still exist, they're no longer relevant, so who cares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-20-2019, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:26:06-07:00","id":1342600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342597#post1342597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that if any of them do still exist, they're no longer relevant, so who cares?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it kind of makes sense, when you consider that even the more recent elders have great difficulty adapting themselves to the modern era. How much more difficult would it be for an Antedeluvian who's been unconscious for the last 3,000 years to become accustomed to the changes that have occurred?<br /> <br /> Sure, they might have Mental attributes reaching the fucking stratosphere, but just because they might be able to learn, doesn't mean they have the time or interest to do so. You can't just pick up a medical book and suddenly understand the field of biology when the last time you were awake, people thought disease was the work of evil spirits!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T09:56:40-07:00","id":1342962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342580#post1342580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's kinda a hypocrite point of view imposed by the elders that know their genealogy up to Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, it's explicable and reconcilable in that the Camarilla doesn't suppress that knowledge directly. The vampiric creation myth -- Caine, the curse, the flood, etc. -- as well as education about the clans, clan founders, and the generation system are all basic parts of any fledgling's education. If their sires don't teach them directly, they learn it from a mentor or peers. Any vampire who's learned their lineage, generation, or can simply count on their fingers can reason for themselves vampires came from somewhere, clans came from somewhere, and all those lineages have to converge somewhere along the way. Neither does the Camarilla expressly deny the existence of methuselahs, but like antediluvians simply explain them as elders of extreme low generation and great age.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla is interested in suppressing, is Noddist lore beyond that as well as various forms of eschatologic belief, chiefly that of Gehenna. I'd wager the methuselah's thirst falls into that category as well, since that plays into Noddist/Gehenna lore. Antediluvians, as in ancient vampires who founded the clans way back when is fine, but &quot;Antediluvians&quot; the prehistoric angry blood gods who are coming to eat everyone during The End Times, is no fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T19:21:44-07:00","id":1343077,"title":"","content":"Descent from Caine is just what the Camarilla wants you to think, man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T20:46:21-07:00","id":1343086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342597#post1342597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's always seemed to me that in-setting, if the Camarilla's argument was that there are no Clan founders, nobody believes that for a second which would leave the Camarilla just looking like obvious dummies for trying to insist that the Clans don't have founders. Which is why I tend to believe they don't try to push that and instead just push the idea that Clan founders weren't particularly powerful, they weren't boogymen and that if any of them do still exist, they're no longer relevant, so who cares?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I've always portrayed the Camarilla's attitude towards the Antediluvians in my games too.<br /> <br /> In the opening fiction for Revised, the vampire tells his intended childe-to-be that the clans are descended from Caine and the Antediluvians. The clan books are all full of legends about their clan founders, passed down from sire to childe. There are tons of Kindred who sign letters with recitations of their lineages all the way back to Caine. There actually aren't that many (any?) specific examples of elders working to suppress knowledge of the Antediluvians among younger Kindred, but there's seemingly a thousand and one exceptions. None of this is helped by the fact how we as readers, and seemingly every character of consequence in the setting, all know the Antediluvians are real. Or how it's so indelibly baked into the game via the concept of generation, which basically every vampire who's not a rube knows about. It also begs the question of just what, according to the supposedly Antediluvian-denying Camarilla, actually <i>did</i> create vampires. I can buy that there isn't a unifying &quot;alternative theory&quot; being actively promoted, but the books don't even give us any example lies Kindred elders tell their childer to answer, &quot;Where do we come from?&quot; The idea just wasn't ever that developed.<br /> <br /> It's much neater to answer that the Camarilla believes in the Antediluvians. They just hold, seemingly quite reasonably, that the clan founders aren't relevant anymore. No one's seen them in millennia. (That isn't quite true, but that is something the elders outright lie about.) The Antes are either dead or in torpors too deep to ever awaken from. Some clans, such as the Ventrue and Malkavians, actively promote the idea their founders are dead and even claim to know how they died.<br /> <br /> Another lie the Camarilla can more subtly promote is that the Antediluvians aren't that powerful. The concept of generation and blood thickening with age may be widely known, but 6+ traits aren't. Most elders aren't casually showing those off, as they're bad for the Masquerade too, and many cities in the New World don't even have elders of sufficient age and generation to hold that coveted sixth dot in a Discipline. Most neonates probably figure traits cap out at 5 even for the Third Generation... if the Antediluvians were around, they'd be worldly, dangerous creatures like any elder, but they wouldn't be all-powerful blood gods. They'd be what elders basically are in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 10-23-2019, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T20:56:22-07:00","id":1343090,"title":"","content":"I think the Camarilla stating they aren't real, denying their existence in public, and executing people who publish copies of the Book of Nod while simultaneously teaching their childer about Caine, having copies of the Book of Nod, and prepping for Gehenna is the most Camarilla thing ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T21:38:05-07:00","id":1343095,"title":"","content":"I tend to think elders want to suppress the Book of Nod out of general principle, because it contains knowledge they want to control access to. But the Chronicle of Shadows turns it from something that's an <i>advantage</i> for them to sit on into something that's <i>dangerous</i> for neonates to read, because it outright says the world is going to end in blood and fire to sate the Antediluvians' hunger. So they pat Jan Pieterzoon on the head and tell him he's a good boy whenever he seizes and burns Noddist texts. (Or, you know, just Dominate him into thinking he's burned them.)<br /> <br /> There was a fun moment in my game where a PC was talking to an older vampire about ghouls. He casually quoted a verse from the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Caroline: She cocks her head. &quot;What is that from?&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;It is scripture, from <i>The Rules of the Canaille</i>. Words of wisdom attributed to our Dark Father's own lips.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caroline: She nods. &quot;Perhaps I'll have a copy someday.&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: The Nosferatu emits a throaty chuckle. &quot;Perhaps, Miss Malveaux. I consider myself fortunate to have read what scattered fragments I have.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caroline: A frown. &quot;There's no collected volume?&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Unfortunately not. Such physical documents endanger the Masquerade by their very nature. And our kind are loath to share.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The PC later met with an elder who brought out a physical copy of the Book of Nod and read some verses from it. <br /> <br /> She still has yet to figure out if that first vampire was lying to her, or had just been lied to himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T09:32:53-07:00","id":1343197,"title":"","content":"You know, I always thought that the Camarilla always said that there were no Antideluvians, because that's a very Masquerade thing to do. Humanity doesn't get to know about vampires because it leads to things like the Inquisiton, makes it harder to feed, etc. Vampires don't get to hear about Antideluvians for the exact same reason - makes it harder for the ancients to control or feed on the young ones. <br /> <br /> Its like... take the Ventrue Antideluvian. Word is, (s)he's dead and gone. But that's exactly what the Ventrue clan members do themselves. Fake their deaths, Dominate you to forget the truth, and pull the strings from the shadows while sipping on blood cocktails from their skull throne. The Camarilla is like a giant vampire-conspiracy onion. Peel back one layer, and there's another conspiracy there, followed by a third layer of string pulling conspiracies, and so on. <br /> <br /> Gangrel, with their feral nature and animalistic tendencies, make poor fits for the conspiracy onion. Naturally, most fit better wild and free in the Anarch Baronies than trying to play the leashed hound, so they naturally gravitate that direction. Fundamentally, that's what its down to. Before V5, there wasn't really a choice between Anarch or Cam, but there is now. Everything else, the abuse and disdain, is just noise and friction on the way there.<br /> <br /> Well, that, or the Sabbat. Feral hunters seem to fit with the diablarie-seeking theme of this sect. <br /> <br /> ((As an aside, the three sects kind of remind me of the three Evils in D&amp;D now. Tyrannical devils and their hierarchy, chaotic demons with dozens of lords, and the greedy daemons playing both sides for their payout.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T12:05:51-07:00","id":1456446,"title":"","content":"Well, if one clan has herd mentality is Gangrel. Most are conformists and just don't want to go taking action and making revolution, and neither do they want to be barked with orders by people they don't know or don't respect. So when a big chunk of their Clan (at least in levels of prestige and respect) says screw it and deserts Camarilla, most probably though 'okay then, if I got the net security of my Clan, I don't really care where we go'. Funny thing is they wouldn't make the Anarch Revolt 1 or 2, but now that there is a Anarch sect through and through where they can nestle themselves, that's where they will find they cool shade and fresh water. <br /> <br /> About the Camarilla Antediluvian Issue, I do think they would say Antediluvians do not exist most times, like &quot;pfff vampires aren't THAT old&quot;, not that powerful, mythological or etc., and I imagine most lineage citing vampires would stop at their House founder, not Clan founder. Like a grand-childe of Jan Pieterzoon would stop at Hardestadt and not go any further. With that, most lineages would stop at the Medieval period I assume. Most elders would probably say that no one is certain of the origins of the Kindred (Cainite is such and old and superstitious term, some might argue), which they aren't really, and that most Clan Founders (if there is such a thing) are dead, forgotten relics of ages past, more shrouded in myth than any facts, like the prophets and gods in most European religions. So all and all is a &quot;don't think about it, no one cares&quot; kind of deal.<br /> Another point about this is that Camarilla acts like an association, where each vampire scratches another's back, so mostly they would be equals in theory. In lieu of this, I think most Elders wouldn't go showing off their herculean powers, mostly making a social dance of superiority to their fellows. At this point you can see 'okay, there are novices, journeyman and masters in this' (neonates, ancillae and elders right?), and it's alright, but what if this was true, and there were actually ultra-masters, and super hyper mega blast masters? Gods incarnate? The whole scheme would feel like a terribly shitty deal, and all the political game of the Camarilla would feel irrelevant. Besides... fear of these godly beings, and the full-on belief in them, is a Sabbat thing.... <br /> Camarilla does with Sabbat (and the opposite probably is true) what McCarthyism did in USA. Any relation with the material brands you then and there. Well, it actually sounds like a Farenheit 451 now.... or Brave New World. Besides, Camarilla acts modern and secular, Nodism is religions babble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T12:41:35-07:00","id":1456448,"title":"","content":"The odd thing for me is thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;We're the Cam, we are the government for all vampires, We have seven clans!&quot;<br /> &quot;seven clans? But there's at least 13 clans out there&quot;<br /> &quot;Shut up&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I could believe that the 7 clans are simply more demographically successful than the other 6; The OG 7 are more generalist while the others are very specialist and thus there's a lot more room for Toreador than there are Assamite or Giovanni. But the issue is that later books went on to blow the horn and announce how the other six clans are huge and that there's more corpse-fuckers and nightmare surgeons than there ever needed to be. But the point is what does it even mean to be &quot;in the cam&quot; or to &quot;leave the cam&quot; when the cam claims everyone and many vampires claim to be cam despite not being on the special list. This goes especially for very disunited clans like the Gangrel and Brujah, who would never wholesale claim belonging to or rejection from a sect. If the Ventrue or Tremere decided to leave the cam for whatever nonsensical reason, they have the collectivization to do so together. But the Gangrel/Brujah? Dick doesn't speak for Harry and Harry doesn't speak for dave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-09-2021, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T13:26:06-07:00","id":1456453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456448#post1456448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odd thing for me is thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;We're the Cam, we are the government for all vampires, We have seven clans!&quot;<br /> &quot;seven clans? But there's at least 13 clans out there&quot;<br /> &quot;Shut up&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And one of those 13 was explicitly banned from entry in 1528, to boot.<br /> <br /> (Perhaps polite kindred society just unanimously voted that the Giovanni and co don't count as an actual clan, per say and there are only 12 now.)<br /> <br /> &quot;All vampires are Camarilla. No exceptions. Except the inbred corpse-fuckers. And the Ravnos, who we'd rather just set on fire the moment they show. And the Lasombra antitribu aren't allowed to sit at the table with us. Also, apparently despite our governorship being absolute and automatic, you can opt out of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> I assume that to not be counted as a Camarilla clan or to &quot;leave&quot; just means you get no primogen or special clan-wide benefits whatever, but you're still counted as a &quot;citizen&quot;. Clan Gangrel didn't leave, because they aren't centralised enough for it and it's not a thing, anway. It was the individual gangrel with titles and positions who quit in protest over a disagreement over governent policy.<br /> <br /> For some reason, I get the impression that V5 is going to end up with all 13 actually somewhat present in the Camarilla by the end. The Lasombra are official (even though for some reason they didn't just do the obvious thing and acknowledge the antitribu) The independents are mostly there. Assamites joined, Church of Set is a thing, and the Hecata are gearing up for the end of the Promise.<br /> <br /> I'm somewhat surprised that Camarilla Tzimisce aren't encouraged or more tolerated. Distaste aside, if I were running a Cam domain, I would want vicissitude. Very useful for maintaining the masquerade when you can make yourself age, create a fake family and then alter your appearance to become your own grandkid or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-09-2021, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T17:26:48-07:00","id":1456477,"title":"","content":"Irrc, in Lore of the Clans, it said that the Gangrel joined mainly in the hope of using the other clans as canon-fodder for their enemies. It could be that they left simply because that never worked out the way they intended. The other clans are simply better at social manipulation than the Gangrel are, by a wide margin. So it was the Gangrel who ended up being the canon-fodder of the other clans.<br /> <br /> The surprising thing is that the Gangrel didn't realize sooner that the other clans, especially the High Clans, had turned this whole use-the-other-clans-as-cannon-fodder plan completely on its head.<br /> <br /> Possibly the reason it took so long is because it was mainly younger Gangrel who got used as canon-fodder. The older Gangrel spend huge chunks of time wandering the forests, and probably only slowly received word that the plan wasn't working out at Gangrel gatherings. It was an experiment they kept plugging away at because their lives are slow-motion things, and because it only cost them neonates, which they can create at will.<br /> <br /> EVENTUALLY they went, well this experiment isn't working, screw it, dropping the Camarilla, but it took waaayyyy longer than it would have for creatures who don't live in slow-motion, and who actually care about their children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T17:41:03-07:00","id":1456479,"title":"","content":"*Reads Thread Title*<br /> Because their subscription ran out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T18:29:44-07:00","id":1456484,"title":"","content":"I think the Gangrel left because they felt like Gehenna was coming and the Camarilla wasn\u2019t doing anything to stop it. But I could be wrong about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T02:45:21-07:00","id":1456510,"title":"","content":"I guess the Gangrel left so easily because the Camarilla is really centred around the Tremere, the Toreador, and the Ventrue. Going by the Clanbooks, the other Clans seem to have a distinctly lesser position, with many members existing only on the periphery of the Camarilla. Xaviar\u2019s call to leave played right into a common and popular sentiment among the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342589#post1342589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few points.<br /> Third, the Camarilla's &quot;public&quot; stance is less &quot;the Antedeluvians don't exist&quot;, and more &quot;the Antedeluvians are not RELEVANT&quot;. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1343086#post1343086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's much neater to answer that the Camarilla believes in the Antediluvians. They just hold, seemingly quite reasonably, that the clan founders aren't relevant anymore. No one's seen them in millennia. (That isn't quite true, but that is something the elders outright lie about.) The Antes are either dead or in torpors too deep to ever awaken from. Some clans, such as the Ventrue and Malkavians, actively promote the idea their founders are dead and even claim to know how they died.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1343197#post1343197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is like a giant vampire-conspiracy onion. Peel back one layer, and there's another conspiracy there, followed by a third layer of string pulling conspiracies, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that the Camarilla\u2019s rather thin policy of denial of the existence of the Antediluvians was put in place in order to prohibit open existence of cults and groups of Vampires revering and serving/supporting their Clan Founder. In the begone history it used to be that the Clans openly followed their particular Founder's will and directions. The Camarilla Elders (and possibly Methuselahs) desperately sought to prevent this from happening again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1343197#post1343197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its like... take the Ventrue Antideluvian. Word is, (s)he's dead and gone. But that's exactly what the Ventrue clan members do themselves. Fake their deaths, Dominate you to forget the truth, and pull the strings from the shadows while sipping on blood cocktails from their skull throne. The Camarilla is like a giant vampire-conspiracy onion. Peel back one layer, and there's another conspiracy there, followed by a third layer of string pulling conspiracies, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never made sense to me that the 3<sup>rd</sup> Generation Founder with mastery over Presence, Dominate, and Fortitude would be simply felled after being ambushed. And are there not 4<sup>th</sup> Generation Ventrue Methuselahs sired after the fall of the Second City?<br /> It makes sense that the Founder of the Clan of rulers would choose to fade into the background. What better way to have sway over the Kindred societies, than to influence and control the Clan Ventrue from behind the scenes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1342600#post1342600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it kind of makes sense, when you consider that even the more recent elders have great difficulty adapting themselves to the modern era. How much more difficult would it be for an Antedeluvian who's been unconscious for the last 3,000 years to become accustomed to the changes that have occurred?<br /> <br /> Sure, they might have Mental attributes reaching the fucking stratosphere, but just because they might be able to learn, doesn't mean they have the time or interest to do so. You can't just pick up a medical book and suddenly understand the field of biology when the last time you were awake, people thought disease was the work of evil spirits!</div> </div> </div> </div>3<sup>rd</sup> Generation Vampires could easily have Vampires or Ghouls (Not Ghouls of Antediluvians, but those belonging to other Vampires. Now that I think of it, is there any mention in VtM of Antediluvians having their own Ghouls?) whose designated role would be to quickly acquaint them with relevant issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-10-2021, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T03:57:41-07:00","id":1456514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456510#post1456510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3<sup>rd</sup> Generation Vampires could easily have Vampires or Ghouls (Not Ghouls of Antediluvians, but those belonging to other Vampires. Now that I think of it, is there any mention in VtM of Antediluvians having their own Ghouls?) whose designated role would be to quickly acquaint them with relevant issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Absimiliard's Gehenna Rex count? But seriously, the Book of Nod does mention ghouls in the First City:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Book of Nod</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Below all Kindred were the Children of Seth, that is to say the humans, except for one. That one was the Master of Servants, the original one-who-serves, called Jabal in some myths. Jabal was equal to one of Caine\u2019s Grandchilder because he was so close to Caine. There was very little of Jabal\u2019s own blood in his body, it was all mostly the Blood of Caine.<br /> <br /> Those-who-serve, the latter-day ghouls, were the next lowest rung, followed by all mortal servants who attended the Kindred. The rest - those who farmed, labored, etc. - were the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26959-tofana-by-l-oreal","name":"Tofana by L'Oreal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T04:04:28-07:00","id":1456515,"title":"","content":"Quite a number of other antideluvians could have felled Ventrue. 10 fortitude isn't invincibility in the face of someone with 10 potence (It probably looks like an ordinary fist fight, really) and Ventrue are not famed for their detection/escape abilities. Do note that if we don't use ventrue's hypothetical 10 fort as &quot;plot device&quot; and just use abilities as listed and scale large weapons accordingly, Antideluvians would be seriously threatened even the smaller modern cannons, nevermind the stuff you'd find on tanks (which are in turn dwarfed by the guns people used to put on ships)<br /> <br /> (I hold to the belief that the weak of nightmares was all chimistry) <br /> Now, while that might not necessarily be correct, it's likely that neonates can experiment with their own levels of potence/fortitude and extrapolate &quot;if 5 fortitude's like this, 10 fortitude aught to be twice as strong, right? That's not too scary&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: The Cam denying Antes. <br /> The Cam is smart. Adamantely denying that something exists creates suspicions, reasoning that something's harmless creates reassurance. The Cam denies &quot;antideluvians&quot; and doesn't like the term because it has connotations. It's like using a racist slur around anti-racists. People'll think you're dangerous. At best, you're showing anti-establishment tendancies, at worst, you're sharing heresy and treason. In a conspiratorial society like vampires where cults are a threat and everyone needs to support the bottom line or else things'll go to shit, that's unacceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T09:32:35-07:00","id":1456535,"title":"","content":"The Inner Circle provides cover for the Antedeluvians because that's their job, of course, of course. To learn more, ask your pack's Priest or Ductus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T10:55:27-07:00","id":1456539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456515#post1456515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a number of other antideluvians could have felled Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">The official version according to clan Ventrue members states that he may have been destroyed outside of the walls of the Second City. Blaming the Brujah Antediluvian - strangely, the Brujah denying this...<br /> The porblem is:<br /> Those 4th Gen Ventrue who running around, not the mention the whole Danava Bloodline (actually I think its true they are the &quot;True Ventrue... the Ven-True... ouch, sorry, had too. And the &quot;Ventrue&quot; are an errant bloodline of Clan Danava) who claim, they are protecting the sleeping Antediluvian who they call &quot;Veddartha&quot; (and there is a Veddartha, the Younger, like Hardestat who sired Maltheas and who is an Iconnu)<br /> Artemis Orthia was embraced around 5000 BC like Medon, her broodmate, so with a bit of a strech she and her &quot;brother&quot; fits in the 2nd City death story<br /> But then it becomes... murky at best</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">Around 3000 BC the dead Antediluvian Embraced Arakur of Ur in ancient Summer<br /> Mithras was sired in </span>1258 BC somewhere in the territory where Iran is now located (by <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">Veddartha. Maybe he diablerised his way, maybe it was the Antediluvian, who know? But for the sake of argument, because there is nothing except Maltheas's sire that question this, Veddartha indeed could be the Antediluvian, while there is Veddartha, the Younger, possible the progeny of Veddartha the Elder, aka. Ventrue Antediluvian. Would be logicall, really...) </span><br /> Around 700 BC he embraced Alexander in Ancient Greece<br /> Before 480 BC the Antediluvian - dead, remember since the 2nd City... - embraced Tinia, who would come to rule over the Etruscans.<br /> And lastly, before 60 BC he embraced Antonius and Erik Eigermann in Ancient Gaul. Erik Eigermann and his descendants later ruled over Berlin. Antonius and his family ruled over Constantinople.<br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">Nefer-meri-Isis, the monitor of the Followers of Set (g</span>iven her name, she probably originated in Egypt<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">) was Embraced... well we don't know exactly when, but Elihu aka. </span><i>Elias Andronicus</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">, her children died in 1450 CE, so her embrace must have been before that... not much of a help, so she is not much of a proof for a living antediluvian. But even if we put her Embrace around 3000 or 5000 BC still counts somewhat, like Artemis<br /> With Presence and Dominate its easy to convince others, &quot;yeah, our Antediluvian died *sob sob* at the Walls of the 2nd City, that darn Brujah Antediluvian killed him! Never forgive! Never forget! Err... don't mind Antonius... nor the rest. They are... look, just stare that pritty picture, okay? Good lad!&quot;</span><br /> Really, anyone belives the Ventrue Antediluvian died in the Second City, when every Ventrue produly trace and list back their liniage to one of his children (and those Childrens were Embraced after the 2nd City where he suposedly died?)?<br /> Then again, the Lasombra belived they destroyed their Antediluvian... despite the fact, no one saw Gratiano commiting the deed, not fell in to deep slumber, still around and the Archbishop of Rio de Janeiro or jumped Generation (even if he for some reason not lowered his generation to 3rd, and became the &quot;new Antediluvian&quot; like Augustus or Tremere, its a minor miracle no one in the Sabbat wondered... gee... maybe who was Embraced 1130 CE by an Antedliuvian is probably now considered something we are fingting against...? Burn the mfker!!!), and no one in the team were capable to recall what exactly happened in there...<br /> Dominate.. fun lil' Discipline...</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-10-2021, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T15:54:19-07:00","id":1456558,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer the idea Ventrue is dead since it's an interesting plot point if some of the 3rd gen are. I liked the suggested plot hood in beckets diary that the anti's are crimminally overated.<br /> <br /> Back on subject I always got the impression the Gangrels sect alliegance was simular to the nosferatu's. A casual commitement because once you're away from the cities, does it really matter? I mean even their Anarch support seems more based on intra clan tensions rather than ideological commitments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-10-2021, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T17:59:04-07:00","id":1456569,"title":"","content":"My theory is that Ventrue BECAME Dominate. He got so good at it that he can possess any of his progeny at will, and not only take them over, but cause them to temporarily drop to 3rd gen. So when he wants to pop out a baby 4rth gen, he just possesses someone and embraces a 4rth gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T20:42:57-07:00","id":1456576,"title":"","content":"&quot;Our forefather is dead and the Brujah killed him. Let's go and burn Carthage!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-10-2021, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T22:07:10-07:00","id":1456579,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;let's go burn carthage&quot; was purely because the vampires in rome wanted to be the sole super-government to oversee other vampires, and carthage was a competitor that couldn't be around inf that plan was to work.<br /> The other &quot;let's go burn carthage&quot;&quot; rationale was thus &quot;well the mortals are going to do it anyway we might as well get involved.&quot; Maybe there could've been some incidents; perhaps a favoured childer was killed in transport due to a naval conflict. But for the most part it's vampires inflating their own influence and using the conflict for propaganda purposes. I'm half convinced the Baali weren't involved at all in carthage and instead it's ventrue propaganda that the Baali latched onto.<br /> <br /> But back on topic: Camarilla membership isn't that demanding. <br /> I feel very strongly that a lot of writers have anarch sentiments that bleed into their work when it shouldn't. The rebels fighting empire angle doesn't work if you dumb down the empire and do everything to improve the odds of the rebels. As the editions move on this becomes more and more of a problem. The Face needs to meet an effective boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-11-2021, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T22:17:56-07:00","id":1456580,"title":"","content":"Oh, it was almost certainly all about the drachmas; over which city-state would reign over Mediterranean sea trade.<br /> <br /> That the Ventrue's filthy commercial interests overlapped so neatly with fighting infernalists and avenging the clan founder lends itself to a reading in which two of these three things were probably pure propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T08:50:40-07:00","id":1456604,"title":"","content":"Just to double down. <br /> A lot of vampire's dumber decisions are due to real life, or one's own table bleeding into the setting as a whole. There's this cognitive dissonance between vampires and the people who play them. If we forget about today and just talk the 90's/early 2000's, without going too into it/revealing how much i'm talking out my ass, your average vampire player is young, liberal, middle income, and really digs anti-establismhent stuff. Your average vampire is old, rich, conservative, and really wants stability. <br /> <br /> This is why the game started something like 90% of vampires are Camarilla, and most of the few anarchs are just Camarilla with a few different ideas . But of course it played and half or so of the players became anarchs so the writing shifted. Then by revised the cam isn't such a global entity, and even if we just talk about the united states, they've got, like, 65% of the vampire pop (How I got this seemingly arbitrary number: Population of united states, takeaway california, florida and nevada, rounded) and in V5 the Cam is like... well it's basically all gone. <br /> <br /> The gangrel and there cool-wolf look attracted the most anti-establishment players. And of course at that point people are asking &quot;Why are the Gangrel in the Cam if they're all edgy narcissistic loners&quot; alongside &quot;why aren't the anarchs more popular if the cam are always presented so dysfunctional?&quot; (because of course the prince must be the antagonist; a stable city would be boring) <br /> <br /> But y'know, just because you want something to happen doesn't mean it's a good idea. Anyone who's familiar with game design will know that the player needs fun challenges, or else they'll try to work out how to &quot;beat&quot; the game in the most easy (boring) way possible. It's a trap to give the players everything they want. Making the Anarchs more successful is the trap, and giving the Gangrel to the anarchs is another trap (as well as immensely unsatisfying to those who've played loyal cam gangrel)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T15:14:15-07:00","id":1456619,"title":"","content":"You wanna see something funny? Go look in Guide to the High Clans and where it talks about the Death of Ventrue and how much of a Mystery it is....then look at the artwork they used for it...CLEARLY Set jumping Ventrue outside the gates of the Second City. Always found that hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T16:24:18-07:00","id":1456626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456604#post1456604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why the game started something like 90% of vampires are Camarilla, and most of the few anarchs are just Camarilla with a few different ideas . But of course it played and half or so of the players became anarchs so the writing shifted.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that's what happened. I can count on the fingers of one hand the number of times I've even witnessed an Anarch game. It's Camarilla by a large margin, then Sabbat, with Anarchs dead last, and not even a competitive last place.<br /> <br /> In my experience, most STs seem to like the Cammies because the structure gives them a game that is easy to control. A Camarilla game lends itself readily to a World of Warcraft structure, where there are NPCs with exclamation points on their heads and they send you on quests. It's laws also allow STs to reign in the worst impulses of players, since the ST can always declare that the Prince has declared no one is to use explosives even in self-defense, because the attention such use brings is a threat to the masquerade. The control mechanisms of the Camarilla become tools of the ST's control.<br /> <br /> I think the reason they decided to focus on Anarchs is they really wanted to double-down on the &quot;personal horror&quot; angle. They wanted something like the TV/movie stories where someone becomes a monster and they mostly deal with things in almost complete isolation. Their concerns are not being caught by their neighbors and the police. They worry mostly about their monstrous urges giving them away, rather than any larger &quot;sect business&quot;.<br /> <br /> They want to completely move away from the World of Warcraft with dice game model. They want something more like a serious version of the Santa Clarita Diet. Just you and a few others, all of you extremely weak, trying to resist killing people, and scrambling desperately to hide evidence when you do kill.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T16:40:53-07:00","id":1456628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456619#post1456619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wanna see something funny? Go look in Guide to the High Clans and where it talks about the Death of Ventrue and how much of a Mystery it is....then look at the artwork they used for it...CLEARLY Set jumping Ventrue outside the gates of the Second City. Always found that hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it lines up quite well with the whole Osiris was embraced by Typhon (i.e. Ventrue) while Set was embraced by Enoia (so originally 4th Gen Gangrel) but became an Antediluvian by diablerizing Ventrue and renaming himself Set-Typhon (with the implication that Ventrue/Typhon may be influencing or has even outright replaced Set as the dominant personality much as happened with Tremere and Saulot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T21:15:01-07:00","id":1456636,"title":"","content":"Gangrel really seem to like stability and easy-going, so when Anarchs are burning shit down and getting all crazy, I suppose Gangrel wouldn't like all the fuss. Besides, as a territorialist, would you prefer Princes that understands boundaries and might not care for you little domain in a country village, or a bunch of vampire burning mortal blood churning Anarchs moving throught the countryside? Besides, Gangrel (I remember from somewhere and the video about the Clan from the Gentlemans Guide) hate diablerie, they think of it as an abomination, so when Camarilla comes and say let's all relax, go to our domains and not to this cannibalistic thing, they probably were &quot;this is tops&quot;.<br /> There's also the fact that with the Camarilla and the whole shtick of going around being recognized almost worldwide, especially with Status, and just crashing in some safe city a few nights before continue your travels or journeys seem something awesome for a Clan that likes to trek so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T00:59:12-07:00","id":1456640,"title":"","content":"See, to me, Gangrel are mostly the types that only nominally join sects, at most joining the sect of &quot;what I wanted to do anyway&quot;. There are few gangrel who truly align with the ideals of the Camarilla/Anarchs/Sabbat, but there are also very few who are going to go out of their way to piss off the sects. Individuals? especially ones that try to infringe on the Gangrel's interests? Sure. Gangrel are much like Nos; Comfortable on the periphery, they advance and retreat on their own, not with the sect. A hard stance like &quot;we're out of the Camarilla&quot; doesn't suit their modus operandi at all. To top it off, the Gangrel aren't like the Settites or Giovanni, they're naturally not adept at making arrangements as a neutral party, infact they have many disadvantages. A FoS/Gio barony brings prosperity to the local princedom, and they invest enough that they're unlikely to reneg on an agreement. Gangrels don't build up so much, they don't connect so much, and are largely only useful as mercenaries. The Gangrel outside of the Cam are at a massive negotiating disadvantage, because what prince wants his city flooded with difficult to control mercenaries? When they were in the Cam, there was a degree of confidence in both parties. Now that they're out, nobody has reassurance, unless someone gets in with the blood-bond...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T06:37:02-07:00","id":1456656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456636#post1456636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gangrel really seem to like stability and easy-going, so when Anarchs are burning shit down and getting all crazy, I suppose Gangrel wouldn't like all the fuss. Besides, as a territorialist, would you prefer Princes that understands boundaries and might not care for you little domain in a country village, or a bunch of vampire burning mortal blood churning Anarchs moving throught the countryside? Besides, Gangrel (I remember from somewhere and the video about the Clan from the Gentlemans Guide) hate diablerie, they think of it as an abomination, so when Camarilla comes and say let's all relax, go to our domains and not to this cannibalistic thing, they probably were &quot;this is tops&quot;.<br /> There's also the fact that with the Camarilla and the whole shtick of going around being recognized almost worldwide, especially with Status, and just crashing in some safe city a few nights before continue your travels or journeys seem something awesome for a Clan that likes to trek so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an interesting interpretation of the Gangrel because I don't think of the Gangrel as remotely easy going. I think of them as highly aggressive and constantly testing boundaries because they're people who are not going to represent a Prince who cannot enforce their will with brute force and power. Also, I don't think there's any sign they like stability because they're people who are going to know the way of things is to take down the strongest to become the strongest.<br /> <br /> But I've always imagined that the Gangrel have had equal members in the Sabbat, Camarilla, and Independents anyway.<br /> <br /> Why did they join the Camarilla? Probably because it was conveinant to just say, &quot;Sure, man, whatever.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T06:46:49-07:00","id":1456658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456640#post1456640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, to me, Gangrel are mostly the types that only nominally join sects, at most joining the sect of &quot;what I wanted to do anyway&quot;. There are few gangrel who truly align with the ideals of the Camarilla/Anarchs/Sabbat, but there are also very few who are going to go out of their way to piss off the sects. Individuals? especially ones that try to infringe on the Gangrel's interests? Sure. Gangrel are much like Nos; Comfortable on the periphery, they advance and retreat on their own, not with the sect. A hard stance like &quot;we're out of the Camarilla&quot; doesn't suit their modus operandi at all. To top it off, the Gangrel aren't like the Settites or Giovanni, they're naturally not adept at making arrangements as a neutral party, infact they have many disadvantages. A FoS/Gio barony brings prosperity to the local princedom, and they invest enough that they're unlikely to reneg on an agreement. Gangrels don't build up so much, they don't connect so much, and are largely only useful as mercenaries. The Gangrel outside of the Cam are at a massive negotiating disadvantage, because what prince wants his city flooded with difficult to control mercenaries? When they were in the Cam, there was a degree of confidence in both parties. Now that they're out, nobody has reassurance, unless someone gets in with the blood-bond...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I get the impression the Allignement with Anarch is more to do with with it being the most supportive of their modus operendi, antipathy towards the Ventrue and Toreador and outright hatred of the Tremere. the Anarchs are pretty weakly written compared to the other sects but the Gangrels allignement kind of works if you considering it more enviromental than idealogical. Simular how to Tzmisces relationship with the Sabbat because it synergises well with clan culture. The Gangrel don't really seem to resent their elders and more resent other clans Elders.<br /> <br /> I've been playing the idea of giving the anarchs actual insitutions and cultural traits and one if the idea's I had was the Anarch movement had a more Pagan outlook then the Catholic Sabbat and Secular Carmarilla. With the strong Germanic Pagan camp in the Gangrel it would make a lot more sense for them to reject both sects and accept a sect which is naturally more open to alternative origins myths like the Followers of Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T08:43:13-07:00","id":1456671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456658#post1456658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression the Allignement with Anarch is more to do with with it being the most supportive of their modus operendi, antipathy towards the Ventrue and Toreador and outright hatred of the Tremere. the Anarchs are pretty weakly written compared to the other sects but the Gangrels allignement kind of works if you considering it more enviromental than idealogical. Simular how to Tzmisces relationship with the Sabbat because it synergises well with clan culture. The Gangrel don't really seem to resent their elders and more resent other clans Elders.<br /> <br /> I've been playing the idea of giving the anarchs actual insitutions and cultural traits and one if the idea's I had was the Anarch movement had a more Pagan outlook then the Catholic Sabbat and Secular Carmarilla. With the strong Germanic Pagan camp in the Gangrel it would make a lot more sense for them to reject both sects and accept a sect which is naturally more open to alternative origins myths like the Followers of Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'd argue V5 in general is weakly written but i digress. the weird thing is that anarchs just don't work as a global sect, it's at best an umbrella term for neonate movements the local prince is a bit iffy about, so the entirety of anarch clans just doesn't make sense because there's no such thing as the anarch movement on a global scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T08:53:01-07:00","id":1456673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456671#post1456671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'd argue V5 in general is weakly written but i digress. the weird thing is that anarchs just don't work as a global sect, it's at best an umbrella term for neonate movements the local prince is a bit iffy about, so the entirety of anarch clans just doesn't make sense because there's no such thing as the anarch movement on a global scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a global Anarch movement. They control the Anarch Free States in Southern California and other places too. In fact there\u2019s a whole book about it (Anarchs for V5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T09:23:49-07:00","id":1456677,"title":"","content":"Pagan anarchs? I seem to have an understanding as to your leanings. <br /> 1- Everyone but the Tremere hates the Tremere. Nobody's special for hating the Tremere. <br /> 2- All the other Camarilla clans are also present in the anarchs in reasonable number. Fleeing to the Anarchs from the Cam because you hate the Toreador? Guess what. There's more of them here. <br /> 3- Everyone (in universe) likes the Ventrue. They're the most likable clan. Lasombra just wishes he was Ventrue. Facts. <br /> 4-The more traditional Tzmisce that aren't getting into &quot;whacky hijinks&quot; aren't really that bad a cultural fit for the Cam. They're excluded largely because Vicissitude is the subject of much Paranoia and because the Younglings among the Sabbat have really fucked their image. Yes, they like their independence, but that hasn't kept them from Sabbat, who are on a far tighter leash than the Cam are. <br /> 5- By your logic, the Nosferatu should also leave the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T10:15:41-07:00","id":1456680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456658#post1456658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I get the impression the Allignement with Anarch is more to do with with it being the most supportive of their modus operendi, antipathy towards the Ventrue and Toreador and outright hatred of the Tremere. the Anarchs are pretty weakly written compared to the other sects but the Gangrels allignement kind of works if you considering it more enviromental than idealogical. Simular how to Tzmisces relationship with the Sabbat because it synergises well with clan culture. The Gangrel don't really seem to resent their elders and more resent other clans Elders.<br /> <br /> I've been playing the idea of giving the anarchs actual insitutions and cultural traits and one if the idea's I had was the Anarch movement had a more Pagan outlook then the Catholic Sabbat and Secular Carmarilla. With the strong Germanic Pagan camp in the Gangrel it would make a lot more sense for them to reject both sects and accept a sect which is naturally more open to alternative origins myths like the Followers of Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea about paganism among the Anarchs but I would also include Celtic/Wiccan paganism as well as Germanic (and possibly Egyptian for the Ministry; they do still worship Set, after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T11:04:18-07:00","id":1456684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456673#post1456673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is a global Anarch movement. They control the Anarch Free States in Southern California and other places too. In fact there\u2019s a whole book about it (Anarchs for V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>talk about missing the point, i think your looking in the wrong solar system there buddy. also the La free states are not even close to a global sect they're a local sect that's expanding but to suggest that not only are they the entirety of the anarch movement and also comparable to the scope of the cam or even the sabbath is ridiculous. and to address your point just because there's official material doesn't make it good or sensible in fact one of the main criticisms of V5's writing is how much favoritism there is towards the anarch movement so breaking the setting to prop up there favorite isn't out of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T11:34:15-07:00","id":1456685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456684#post1456684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> talk about missing the point, i think your looking in the wrong solar system there buddy. also the La free states are not even close to a global sect they're a local sect that's expanding but to suggest that not only are they the entirety of the anarch movement and also comparable to the scope of the cam or even the sabbath is ridiculous. and to address your point just because there's official material doesn't make it good or sensible in fact one of the main criticisms of V5's writing is how much favoritism there is towards the anarch movement so breaking the setting to prop up there favorite isn't out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it\u2019s official it still counts. Right? Doesn\u2019t matter whether it\u2019s V20 or V5. In fact I would think V5 would count more since it\u2019s the current rule system.<br /> <br /> There is defo an official global Anarch Movement. Whether you think it\u2019s a good thing is a different question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T12:11:14-07:00","id":1456687,"title":"","content":"More points to address<br /> <b>1</b>: The Anarchs are more defined by not fitting in with the establishments of the Cam/Sabbat than they are defined as an establishment in their own right. What does an Anarch city look like? Is it Fascist, Anarchist, Collectivist, theocratic? It could be anything. This theme of the Anarchs not really having a good definition has ran right the way through VTM: The &quot;free states&quot; are a clusterfuck of different people trying different ways to assert power. Anarchs historically didn't even agree on how much they don't like the Cam, with some wanting total revolution and others just wanting a prince more amicable to their goals.<br /> <b>2:</b> V5 may be the current rule system, but <b>A</b>:The first 4 editions had more in common than not, whilst the 5th is a radical departure. If I had four sources telling me Quietus and Thaumaturgy were seperate things, and one source telling me they're the same thing, I'm more inclined to go with the four sources, and <b>B</b>: V5 is not popular here (5:1 in favour of V20, according to the last poll) and many exercise it from their own canons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T12:13:19-07:00","id":1456688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456685#post1456685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it\u2019s official it still counts. Right? Doesn\u2019t matter whether it\u2019s V20 or V5. In fact I would think V5 would count more since it\u2019s the current rule system.<br /> <br /> There is defo an official global Anarch Movement. Whether you think it\u2019s a good thing is a different question.</div> </div> </div> </div>holy shit ma dude can you fucking read? i'm not saying there is no global anarch movement, i'm saying a global anarch movement doesn't make sense, just because something is official in V5 doesn't mean it makes sense. do you comprehend this fucking sentence.<br /> <br /> the LA anarchs aren't a global sect because they're a local sect nines isn't gonna make a desicion that affects the anarchs of antwerp or beijing the La anarchs might want to start a global anarch movement or be an important part of a global anarch movement but they are not a global movement they're the <b><u>LA</u></b> anarchs, you think isaac is concerned about what's going on with the anarchs in berlin? no, he has hollywood to worry about.<br /> <br /> then what is the global anarch movement? a few dozen chat room moderators and a couple of nomadic advisors/activists, that's it. if you think i'm severly underselling the anarch movement because there's no way something that bare bones poses a threath to the cam, i'm not that's just how shitely it's written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T13:17:24-07:00","id":1456692,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that there aren't really any truly global organizations anymore.<br /> <br /> Even before the beckoning, the ability of the sects to concentrate troops in an area was extremely limited because of the masquerade. They could never just pour a hundred armed vampires into a city and overrun it. Post-beckoning, the sects being even semi-global is right out, because there simply aren't enough immensely powerful elders.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the Sects are less global organizations than they are religions or mindsets. The Camarilla is the mindset that the oldest vampires in a given city should rule in a very top-down way. The Anarch is the mindset that age is irrelevant, though what should replace it is extremely vague and varies drastically from city to city and anarch to anarch. The Sabbat is the mindset that Paths of Enlightenment are the only way to avoid wightdom long term, therefore religious leaders who can guide vampires onto Paths of the Enlightenment should lead locally.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Truly global organizations are over post-beckoning, and were never really as global as they pretended to be even pre-beckoning because of the practical limitations of concentrating troops in the face of the masquerade.<br /> <br /> This puts the Anarchs on a much more even footing than they had in previous editions. The Camarilla and Sabbat are now only slightly more organized, and their inability to concentrate troops drastically reduces the effectiveness of their slightly greater organizational ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T13:27:32-07:00","id":1456695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456692#post1456692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that there aren't really any truly global organizations anymore.<br /> <br /> Even before the beckoning, the ability of the sects to concentrate troops in an area was extremely limited because of the masquerade. They could never just pour a hundred armed vampires into a city and overrun it. Post-beckoning, the sects being even semi-global is right out, because there simply aren't enough immensely powerful elders.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the Sects are less global organizations than they are religions or mindsets. The Camarilla is the mindset that the oldest vampires in a given city should rule in a very top-down way. The Anarch is the mindset that age is irrelevant, though what should replace it is extremely vague and varies drastically from city to city and anarch to anarch. The Sabbat is the mindset that Paths of Enlightenment are the only way to avoid wightdom long term, therefore religious leaders who can guide vampires onto Paths of the Enlightenment should lead locally.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Truly global organizations are over post-beckoning, and were never really as global as they pretended to be even pre-beckoning because of the practical limitations of concentrating troops in the face of the masquerade.<br /> <br /> This puts the Anarchs on a much more even footing than they had in previous editions. The Camarilla and Sabbat are now only slightly more organized, and their inability to concentrate troops drastically reduces the effectiveness of their slightly greater organizational ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T14:01:12-07:00","id":1456698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456692#post1456692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that there aren't really any truly global organizations anymore.<br /> <br /> Even before the beckoning, the ability of the sects to concentrate troops in an area was extremely limited because of the masquerade. They could never just pour a hundred armed vampires into a city and overrun it. Post-beckoning, the sects being even semi-global is right out, because there simply aren't enough immensely powerful elders.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the Sects are less global organizations than they are religions or mindsets. The Camarilla is the mindset that the oldest vampires in a given city should rule in a very top-down way. The Anarch is the mindset that age is irrelevant, though what should replace it is extremely vague and varies drastically from city to city and anarch to anarch. The Sabbat is the mindset that Paths of Enlightenment are the only way to avoid wightdom long term, therefore religious leaders who can guide vampires onto Paths of the Enlightenment should lead locally.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Truly global organizations are over post-beckoning, and were never really as global as they pretended to be even pre-beckoning because of the practical limitations of concentrating troops in the face of the masquerade.<br /> <br /> This puts the Anarchs on a much more even footing than they had in previous editions. The Camarilla and Sabbat are now only slightly more organized, and their inability to concentrate troops drastically reduces the effectiveness of their slightly greater organizational ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i'm sorry but that's just a bad take, wrong for many diffrent reasons.<br /> first of whether an organization is global isn't a matter of territory it's a matter of resources, and while territory is a resource it's not the only one or the most important one.<br /> <br /> as for your invasion example: the EU is a global superpower, can it just invade venezuela? no because of regulations. does that make it any less of a global superpower? no, that's ridiculous to even suggest.<br /> i don't know even know what you were even suggesting with those takes<br /> <br /> <br /> the cam was always been a decentrelized global power and while the cam lost alot due to the beckoning it hasn't collapsed or fractured to a point were they're no longer a global power it's definitly an even more decentrilized organization due to the loss of &quot;upper managment&quot; and most cities have gone into a crisis mode but that doesn't mean they stopped being a global power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T14:43:21-07:00","id":1456704,"title":"","content":"There was a theory on the forums long ago that Brujah and his most violent childe, Troile, ambushed Ventrue. And destroyed him, with Troile diablerizing him. Brujah then went underground as the first Antediluvian to have faked his death. To cover the Ventrues honor, Veddharta passed as their Antediluvian for a while. Among other things, this was based on the oldest Brujah 4th generation being about 6 years younger than the youngest Ventrue 4th.<br /> <br /> t was a good theory, but later editions have added more Ventrue Methuselahs and obsoleted it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, White Wolf directly stated that Mithras sire was the Ventrue Antediluvian in Victorian Age Vampire.<br /> <br /> At the end of Revised, Justin Achilli posted on the forums that the Ventrue Antediluvians powers included the ability to return from final death. I remember Dark Ages had a lesser fortitude power that did much the same thing at a great cost. But anyway, Ventue would be spending most of his time in the Shadowlands and only enter the living world occasionally. Now does that sound like someone else we know, who was slain immediately after the fall of the second city?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456628#post1456628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it lines up quite well with the whole Osiris was embraced by Typhon (i.e. Ventrue) while Set was embraced by Enoia (so originally 4th Gen Gangrel) but became an Antediluvian by diablerizing Ventrue and renaming himself Set-Typhon (with the implication that Ventrue/Typhon may be influencing or has even outright replaced Set as the dominant personality much as happened with Tremere and Saulot).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a good match. However, Typhon was described as &quot;<i>possessing no emotion except a cruel humor</i>&quot;, Osiris complained to his wife after his embrace that all his passion had been leached out of him, and without meeting his sire, the disciplines he first developed was Potence, Presence and Celerity. All of which indicates that Typhon was Brujah. All the evidence does indicate that Typhon was diablerized by Set not Troile though.<br /> <br /> Of course, the tales about Set and Troile are exceptionally similar...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T14:55:11-07:00","id":1456705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456704#post1456704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Dark Ages had a lesser fortitude power that did much the same thing at a great cost. </div> </div> </div> </div>are you sure you're not thinking of the protean power &quot;draught of phoenix blood&quot;? because i'm fairly certain there's no fortitude power that let's you return from final death","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T15:03:19-07:00","id":1456707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456705#post1456705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are you sure you're not thinking of the protean power &quot;draught of phoenix blood&quot;? because i'm fairly certain there's no fortitude power that let's you return from final death</div> </div> </div> </div>Cappadocian Mortis-Fortitude combination, maybe? To be honest I only remember it vaguely. Big cost, something about never being able to raise your stats or disciplines again, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T15:13:46-07:00","id":1456708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456707#post1456707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cappadocian Mortis-Fortitude combination, maybe? To be honest I only remember it vaguely. Big cost, something about never being able to raise your stats or disciplines again, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>sounds like <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">draught of phoenix blood</span></span></span>, you gain a generation and loose all powers that exceed the limitations of your new generation except for the resurection power itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T15:17:32-07:00","id":1456709,"title":"","content":"Found it. Blessed Resilience from Clanbook Cappadocian. Needs Fortitude 8, Mortis 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T16:28:07-07:00","id":1456716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456671#post1456671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'd argue V5 in general is weakly written but i digress. the weird thing is that anarchs just don't work as a global sect, it's at best an umbrella term for neonate movements the local prince is a bit iffy about, so the entirety of anarch clans just doesn't make sense because there's no such thing as the anarch movement on a global scale.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I agree but I'm trying to be construtively critical rather than just listing failures-otherwise I'd go blow by blow how stupid fusing necromancy and obetenerbration was. I mostly I agree with this, it's pretty unworkable as it is unless you lean into the total collapse of Sabbat and Carmarilla nation states otherwise Anarch territories are easy pickings. A re-write would require either a psuado dark age setting where the 'sects' are closer to the culture rather than nation state or the anarchs would need a overarching leadership.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456677#post1456677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pagan anarchs? I seem to have an understanding as to your leanings.<br /> 1- Everyone but the Tremere hates the Tremere. Nobody's special for hating the Tremere.<br /> 2- All the other Camarilla clans are also present in the anarchs in reasonable number. Fleeing to the Anarchs from the Cam because you hate the Toreador? Guess what. There's more of them here.<br /> 3- Everyone (in universe) likes the Ventrue. They're the most likable clan. Lasombra just wishes he was Ventrue. Facts.<br /> 4-The more traditional Tzmisce that aren't getting into &quot;whacky hijinks&quot; aren't really that bad a cultural fit for the Cam. They're excluded largely because Vicissitude is the subject of much Paranoia and because the Younglings among the Sabbat have really fucked their image. Yes, they like their independence, but that hasn't kept them from Sabbat, who are on a far tighter leash than the Cam are.<br /> 5- By your logic, the Nosferatu should also leave the Cam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> lol no I like the 3rd ed Carmarilla is best. Least awful vampire society hands down by a mile. I also tend to frown on using the game as a platform for my beliefs anyway.<br /> <br /> 1)Yeah but some clans hate the Tremere on a far more drastic scale Gangrel hatred of the clan is a plot point.<br /> 2) I could imagine they could tolerate individuals as the clan as the issue is the 3 three lording it over the plebian clans in the ivory tower<br /> 3) lol yeah I hear Troile is tsundare for Verdatta and it's all a mistunderstanding. Tzmisce often cries into ventrue body pillow that she/he/it'll never be as awsome as him<br /> 4)Yes thats precisly my point with the comparison<br /> 5)Logic is a strong word since vampiric politics like irl politics isnt rational or logical more accuratly it's possible explanation of how the gangrel might align with the Anarchs<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456680#post1456680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your idea about paganism among the Anarchs but I would also include Celtic/Wiccan paganism as well as Germanic (and possibly Egyptian for the Ministry; they do still worship Set, after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>You could take it even further by drawin on Brujah links with Carthage and Athens to adopt either pagan pantheons or classic greek philisophy. This idea even feeds into my idea of Anarchs having an Athenian style direct democracy on a local level rather than just a less impressive prince<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T18:26:55-07:00","id":1456724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456656#post1456656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's an interesting interpretation of the Gangrel because I don't think of the Gangrel as remotely easy going. I think of them as highly aggressive and constantly testing boundaries because they're people who are not going to represent a Prince who cannot enforce their will with brute force and power. Also, I don't think there's any sign they like stability because they're people who are going to know the way of things is to take down the strongest to become the strongest.<br /> <br /> But I've always imagined that the Gangrel have had equal members in the Sabbat, Camarilla, and Independents anyway.<br /> <br /> Why did they join the Camarilla? Probably because it was conveinant to just say, &quot;Sure, man, whatever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I can see them being overly aggressive too, like a lazy cat and a pissed off bear, maybe some Gangrel are both, maybe the Clan is rich in both types. But except for their own cultures and beliefs, I take them as being more skeptic (when they aren't the pagan superstitious Gangrel), so they mostly join sects for individual or pack convenience. Although I don't see them as being more pro-Clan than pro-Sect as Nosferatu are, they would probably be &quot;hey Feral friend, your from the other sect, so there's a pretty good reason for me to gut you open and take your teeth as trophies&quot;. As such I don't believe they would want to bring political change (not to others, they are kind of self-centered in a 'don't care about your business' way), so they only act when it is about them or their allies, and mostly would enter or leave the sect, instead of making moves. <br /> And it does make sense for the one of the most warmongering (if their most aggressive side is to be taken as a big part of the Clan) that literally becomes monstrous when frenzy, who's powers are pretty showy, and don't like to act all polished and human around, go the fuck off the Camarilla once the siege closes in with the new security rules, Inquisition threat and etc.. Like, yeah they are now cramping their lifestyle by saying &quot;would you mind not act like a frigging caveman, walking in bands, turning into dogs, talking to pigeons and howling?&quot;. So Anarch it is. Well, this would add up to the other following Xaviar out.<br /> I remember Morrow the Sage in Under the Black Cross, who crossed so many miles just to arrive at Jurgen's court to say &quot;hey, don't go to our land, and if you go to war you will do that and it's going to stink for you and be a bore for us&quot;, and they didn't do much else, so I kind get this idea that Gangrel just want to be left alone, which is kind of boring for a game, but makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> But yeah, why they joined Camarilla in the first place would be (for me) an important point to think, as it would give the parameter that was broken and initiated their fall-out from the Cam. And yeah, we already touched upon the topic in this thread, but I believe there is more to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T04:17:14-07:00","id":1456746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456716#post1456716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah I agree but I'm trying to be construtively critical rather than just listing failures-otherwise I'd go blow by blow how stupid fusing necromancy and obetenerbration was. I mostly I agree with this, it's pretty unworkable as it is unless you lean into the total collapse of Sabbat and Carmarilla nation states otherwise Anarch territories are easy pickings. A re-write would require either a psuado dark age setting where the 'sects' are closer to the culture rather than nation state or the anarchs would need a overarching leadership.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>the problem is that to salvage V5's writing you pretty much have to throw everything into the thrash and start over and if you do that you can do pretty much anything. so the only real advise i can give is: &quot;try again&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T05:39:23-07:00","id":1456749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456716#post1456716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah I agree but I'm trying to be construtively critical rather than just listing failures-otherwise I'd go blow by blow how stupid fusing necromancy and obetenerbration was. I mostly I agree with this, it's pretty unworkable as it is unless you lean into the total collapse of Sabbat and Carmarilla nation states otherwise Anarch territories are easy pickings. A re-write would require either a psuado dark age setting where the 'sects' are closer to the culture rather than nation state or the anarchs would need a overarching leadership.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> lol no I like the 3rd ed Carmarilla is best. Least awful vampire society hands down by a mile. I also tend to frown on using the game as a platform for my beliefs anyway.<br /> <br /> 1)Yeah but some clans hate the Tremere on a far more drastic scale Gangrel hatred of the clan is a plot point.<br /> 2) I could imagine they could tolerate individuals as the clan as the issue is the 3 three lording it over the plebian clans in the ivory tower<br /> 3) lol yeah I hear Troile is tsundare for Verdatta and it's all a mistunderstanding. Tzmisce often cries into ventrue body pillow that she/he/it'll never be as awsome as him<br /> 4)Yes thats precisly my point with the comparison<br /> 5)Logic is a strong word since vampiric politics like irl politics isnt rational or logical more accuratly it's possible explanation of how the gangrel might align with the Anarchs<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You could take it even further by drawin on Brujah links with Carthage and Athens to adopt either pagan pantheons or classic greek philisophy. This idea even feeds into my idea of Anarchs having an Athenian style direct democracy on a local level rather than just a less impressive prince</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a great idea. Like Pericles (Pericles of Athens not Pericles the Shakespeare character). Critias from Chicago by Night would love that\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T06:45:54-07:00","id":1456754,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> you should cool it before they descend. <br /> <br /> I think the original core 7 members of the Cam make a lot of sense, not completely; they really should try to be all encompassing, but I can understand why they picked who they did and excluded who they didn't. The OG 7 are the generalists, the clans that are found in all open sects. <br /> <br /> -The Followers of Set need room to do their masquerade risking cult activities, and are sketchy enough that they shouldn't be afforded too many protections, but they are also friendly enough and &quot;landed&quot; enough to form a close and mutually beneficial relationship with. <br /> -Nobody likes the Ravnos and many'd be happy to see them wiped out. <br /> -The Lasombra mostly went hard into being anarchs, which is a good pretense to keep the rest of them away from power. &quot;ventrue, but really aggressive&quot; isn't something you want in a stable domain. <br /> -The Assamites are just a threat. An entire bloodline who think they're the Law? No thanks. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Gangrel (and Brujah) really don't have such problems. They, as far as vampires go, are easy to get along with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T08:29:54-07:00","id":1456761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456754#post1456754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> you should cool it before they descend.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>you called?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T09:42:12-07:00","id":1456765,"title":"","content":"I really did like LORE OF THE CLANS' explanation. The Gangrel thought that they would be using the Camarilla as a bulwark against all of their enemies and then somehow ended up on the frontlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T10:59:09-07:00","id":1456768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456765#post1456765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really did like LORE OF THE CLANS' explanation. The Gangrel thought that they would be using the Camarilla as a bulwark against all of their enemies and then somehow ended up on the frontlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the first idea is plain dumb. <br /> The result is... well, why do they care? It's not like the Ventrue are enslaving Gangrel elders into becoming their meatshields. If the Neonates end up as fodder, that's their problem. The clan isn't known for coddling their childer, so why now?<br /> <br /> Here's a stray thought<br /> The Gangrel Joined the Camarilla because if they didn't, they'd be hunted down in the face of modernity. Their anti-civilization stance worked so well... before the renaissance. In the early modern period, they realized that going against the flow was futile, and they'd be persecuted for their old ways. With no way to beat them, the only option was to join them.<br /> <br /> 500 years later and they're apparently forgetting this and thinking they need to go their own way again, and the whole clan needs to get on the bandwagon? If the early modern was a warning, surely the information age should've fortified the fear, right? The Gangrel leaving the Cam is like a nation dependent on imports baring all trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T11:55:59-07:00","id":1456772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456765#post1456765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really did like LORE OF THE CLANS' explanation. The Gangrel thought that they would be using the Camarilla as a bulwark against all of their enemies and then somehow ended up on the frontlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reason they took so long to decide it wasn't working was because the clan is so disorganized. Elder Gangrel spend years, even decades wandering to the forests, only occasionally attending gatherings and getting news.<br /> <br /> And that news would have been mixed for a long time. There would have been some Gangrel complaining about being used as canon-fodder, but others would have been saying things like, &quot;yeah, this Camarilla thing is working out great. I've been made Sheriff, and I've got a whole squad of neonates under my command, some of them High Clans. When things get ugly, I can order Ventrue, Toreador, and Tremere to investigate and take all the risks for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> EVENTUALLY they'd realize that the number of times the Gangrel were being used exceeded the number of times Gangrel got to use others by a substantial margin, but I can easily see that taking centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T14:05:57-07:00","id":1456784,"title":"","content":"For me, the Revised explanation was enough: the Camarilla lies about the Antediluvians and won't take them seriously (at least not openly). With what the Clan had become aware of, they couldn't stay around the hypocrites any longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T14:11:56-07:00","id":1456830,"title":"","content":"The take I use in my campaign is it was mostly just a case of mutual disinterest. The Gangrel had little use for anything going on in the city and the Camarilla had zero interest in expending resources protecting the territory the Gangrels actually cared about.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not even a divorce, that would require more energy than either party has for the situation... its more just one of them started spending more and more time on the road for their job and lets most of the calls from the other go to voicemail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T02:55:49-07:00","id":1456865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456746#post1456746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the problem is that to salvage V5's writing you pretty much have to throw everything into the thrash and start over and if you do that you can do pretty much anything. so the only real advise i can give is: &quot;try again&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I have to try and be constructive, not in the least because I don't want a repeat show of d&amp;d 5th where they got props simply for not being 4th because feedback was &quot;too toxic.&quot;. I'm hoping if feedback is contructive v6 will have a lot more spit and polish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T03:37:45-07:00","id":1456867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456830#post1456830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The take I use in my campaign is it was mostly just a case of mutual disinterest. The Gangrel had little use for anything going on in the city and the Camarilla had zero interest in expending resources protecting the territory the Gangrels actually cared about.<br /> l.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it works like that. At all. Before we even get into the issue of &quot;disinterest&quot;<br /> The Camarilla doesn't expend resources to protect one another. The Camarilla exists (on paper) only to protect vampires from mortals (and to protect old vampires from young vampires through appearing to moderate powers of each.) <br /> There's no sect-wide proclamation that they need to defend eachother's territories. That's up to individual princes and gangrel to work out. <br /> <br /> Now. &quot;disinterest&quot; <br /> That's dangerous thinking. <br /> <br /> To butcher some financial terms, Vampires need &quot;Confidence&quot; to work with one another. Near every vampire is a blood sucking sociopath, and near every vampire will implicate their peers if they were ever to be brought down by mortals. Prestation is an investment; you can only work with characters you trust, and you can only have trust with people bound by the same rules as you. Once you have that, Both parties can build up credit and collatoral and deepen their bonds: If you owe someone, you become an investment that they need to protect. If someone owes you, and they're well embeded within the system, then you have an asset. <br /> <br /> The Gangrel leaving the Cam creates a lot of issues in this virtuous cycle for the Gangrel. <br /> First, they're not bound by the same rules as you. The chance of someone reneging on an arrangement has skyrocketed. Even if they don't go back on their word, the value of each favour is undermined by the increased likelihood of refusing to honour an arrangement. <br /> Second, they're outsiders, so you're doing a favour for them by even talking to them. A Gangrel has to look up to every Camarilla member they do a favour for. Nobody wants that kind of social deficit. The help of an outsider is more often than not less valuable than an insider. Questions on &quot;why are you going to Gary the Gangrel rather than Terry the Toreador&quot; will really harm your prestige. <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lastly, all this prevents the build up of credit and collateral. The Gangrel no longer has the confidence to build up a valuable domain near Camarilla territory; the Prince can decide the Gangrel's a risk and take back everything it's ever given to the Gangrel for the good of the sect. Because of this, the Gangrel is going to have even less collateral, so the Gangrel can't be trusted because they don't have as much to lose; You're not going to give a blood sucking sociopath a loan of a million dollary-doos if he only has land worth 10k and no steady job. The risk is too great. <br /> <br /> The Gangrel leaving the Cam is only bad for the Gangrel. There are no positives. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T12:13:19-07:00","id":1456896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456865#post1456865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well I have to try and be constructive, not in the least because I don't want a repeat show of d&amp;d 5th where they got props simply for not being 4th because feedback was &quot;too toxic.&quot;. I'm hoping if feedback is contructive v6 will have a lot more spit and polish.</div> </div> </div> </div>i totally get were you're comming from but it's just so clearly that alot of issues with V5 was something with it's development process went wrong which we can't criticize because we don't know it. best we can do is guess what went wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T12:36:48-07:00","id":1456898,"title":"","content":"5th edition DnD was a big improvement over 3.5. I miss being able to allocate points into skills, but it's much more positive than negative.<br /> <br /> V5... aren't we still getting banned for being honest about it? archderd, I feel like i'm in a suspense thriller watching you be so open with no redtext in sight.<br /> But... yeah<br /> Revised has some <i>fucking stupid shit, </i> but it also has some good/necessary/praiseworthy changes.<br /> My favourite changes for V5 are like...<br /> It's great that some flaws are placed with relevant backgrounds so they can work as &quot;anti-backgrounds&quot;<br /> Grafitti to mark Domain? Great idea.<br /> Coterie background points? I mean the execution's a bit wobbly as it obviously all has to go into Chasse but the idea itself is nice and the execution adds more to the game than it takes away..<br /> and... Er... ah... yeah that's it. Some other good ideas are directly shot down by the bad things attached/terribly executed.<br /> <br /> I'd like to think of it as Week of Nightmares 2: eletric boogaloo. It's all chimistry.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel wouldn't leave the Cam, and nor would the Brujah. The Assamites deserve far more resistance from the Camarilla, and the Lasombra stuff is just completely and utterly <i>wrong</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T12:45:40-07:00","id":1456901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456898#post1456898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">archderd, I feel like i'm in a suspense thriller watching you be so open with no redtext in sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>i hope you like the show, but i've been talking shit about V5 for a while now and haven't gotten so much as a warning so i'm gonna keep talking shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T09:26:25-07:00","id":1456970,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1061/1924/products/Sleeping_Emoji_grande.png?v=1571606036\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ......<br /> ..... oh what? Oh yeah, getting back to it, maybe the Gangrel are making a bet of some kind, like let's see what is gonna go when we remove our status as an official Clan of the Cam.<br /> Maybe they felt they suffered more abuse from the Status and Boon system than it was worth, beside they probably suffered a lot of persecution for their Banes and Disciplines which are Masquerade threatening. So yeah, I can see a &quot;don't mind don't care for my sect&quot; Gangrel going with the rest simply because it doesn't make that much of a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T10:13:26-07:00","id":1456971,"title":"","content":"Going back to that thing about the Gangrel being pissed off that their childer are being used as shock troops, there is precedent for it. It\u2019s why they\u2019re still pissed at the Tremere. Being descended from the dude who went on a rampage against the warlocks when the clan found out their fledglings were being kidnapped for gargoyle material is considered impressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;They say that we\u2019re a cold, hard lot. We abandon our childer and let them live or die on their own. It\u2019s true, to a point. There\u2019s also no mother like a Gangrel, and once the child has successfully survived the fall from the nest, a Gangrel sire can be like a lioness. The Tremere had been kidnapping our childer, twisting them into abominations. We were promised [joining the Camarilla] was a way to stop that from happening \u2014 a way to force the Tremere to give it up and seek peace.&quot; - V20, Lore of the Clans </div> </div> </div>Your kids are getting killed because they suck at surviving? Sucks to be them, pick a better childe next time.<br /> Somebody is systematically attacking your kids or getting them killed? <i>Now</i> the clan is pissed.<br /> <br /> Similarly, back then the other clans brushed off the Gangrels losses and concerns about the Tremere, so after repeatedly getting their concerns and opinions dismissed and being talked down to, the older Gangrel who aren't already done with the &quot;high clans'&quot; shit may well've decided the Camarilla wasn't worth it.<br /> <br /> They've also been arguing about the decision at gatherings since the decision to join was made (a decision they almost didn't agree to). A lot of them never agreed, and those that did were often very meh about it.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Gangrel <i>were</i> definitely a Camarilla clan because that was how 1e worked, and the Gangrel quit because writers felt it was a good twist and/or that the Gangrel were too individualistic and decentralised to make sense as a cam clan. It's not really so deep, I think. Nevertheless, that's the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-16-2021, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T14:32:17-07:00","id":1456981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456971#post1456971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Your kids are getting killed because they suck at surviving? Sucks to be them, pick a better childe next time.<br /> Somebody is systematically attacking your kids or getting them killed? <i>Now</i> the clan is pissed.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes an emotional sense. Most Gangrel don't even have the means to coddle their progeny. It's not like a Toreador where they can put their progeny in a room in their mansion and bring them food until they adapt.<br /> <br /> They are on the road or the forest and turn a hitchhiker or a camper. Abandoning them spares them a lot of emotional pain, since they don't become emotionally attached to a person who has a low chance of survival no matter what they do.<br /> <br /> So they abandon their progeny and then come back to them if they have survived on their own long enough that the sire can feel safe emotionally bonding with them. Effectively Gangrel have a period when they are not yet considered True Gangrel, but once they achieve True Gangrel status, Gangrel sires become just as attached to them as any other sire.<br /> <br /> Once that happens, Gangrel sires become especially pissed at someone killing their progeny, because you completely subverted the simple trick they had used to spare themselves emotional pain in the first place. The progeny had survived an entire month without even knowing all the rules. The progeny had the right stuff. LOVING THEM WAS SUPPOSED TO BE SAFE NOW. RRRAAAAAAAHHHRRR!!!!!!!!!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 08-16-2021, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T16:30:16-07:00","id":1456984,"title":"","content":"That is indeed a very interesting way too look at it! The Gangrel are really into the trope of not liking change at their surroundings or themselves, and if it changes (in a bad way) they will either lash out or move-on, they don't like to be too confrontational, like an animal, they prefer to bark or bite if it gets too close, but don't much like to have to make slow changes, longtime plans and dragged confrontations. It's like they adapt, but at the same time they don't want to change, it is a weird conformism. And they aren't accustomed to dangerous uncertainty, they aren't daredevils, if they are wanderers it doesn't mean they travel without thought or care, they might like to have no worries, and that is why they prepare. Although there is no law right? So some might just be simply carefree.<br /> Of course, there are the Gangrel who are in the perpetual state of lashing out, like Arnulf, who seems forever threatened (personally, ideologically or politically) by all the complex and interdependent societies that are growing up, and so they go to war. Some Gangrel seem hellbent after something they deeply believed, loved or liked was taken or threatened, and these are the most warring of them. <br /> <br /> So yeah, in the end, they are pretty fucking pissed when their lifestyle or interests are meddled with, maybe not in a possessive way like Tzimisce, but in a personal manner. This translates perfectly to their progeny getting gunked and they getting mad<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T17:52:00-07:00","id":1456987,"title":"","content":"Maybe they just finally had enough of hearing &quot;Who let the dogs out?&quot; Whenever they arrived at the Elysium...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T00:59:36-07:00","id":1457008,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel really aren't that bad at making money and building up territory (with animals) . They can ghoul and accumulate resources just the same as any other vampire. They do benefit from being able to take territory other vampires would struggle in. The Stereotype of poor, peniless Gangrel really only works for the very young or the vampires that actively eschew wealth for... whatever reason. (I suppose if your luck hates you and you get a facial animal feature, that can knock you down a bit, but you can still acquire great resources through ghouls and other proxies) <br /> <br /> The Low Clan/High Clan divide is just a bit of prejudice. Actively building a sect around it is just short-sighted lunacy. The worst you could do is not invite the low clans to parties, or give them bad seating arrangements. if you wanted to go further with it the &quot;high clans&quot; would eventually face the possibility of a slaughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T02:02:58-07:00","id":1457009,"title":"","content":"From the two games I've played in where this was covered (UK masquerade back in the past times and a table top a few years ago) the response from most Gangrel players seems to be the same.<br /> It went along the lines of. <br /> Plot dump - &quot;Xavier's met an antideluvian, but nobody believes him so now the clan is out.&quot; <br /> Pcs - &quot;Who's Xavier? I'm quite comfy being prince/sheriff/well to do local here so I think I'll stay thank you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could see mad defections in the USA following the clan novel events, but the only way I could see a while clean leaving is if the other clans all got together and booted them out (forcibly if needed).<br /> Same for the Brujah. The Ventrue could be strongly campaigning the other clans to give them the kick, but to think the whole clan just defected on the day so of one (notable) elder doesn't fit with the image of vampires as generally insular, power mad, crotchety old so and so's that don't like change and think everyone else is out to get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T02:36:19-07:00","id":1457012,"title":"","content":"Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavians... I don't really see those guys following the crowd. The Toreador also have plenty of Avant Gardes and individualists amongst their cliques, and the Nosferatu are a clan before a sect so it doesn't matter where on the political spectrum you go.<br /> There will be plenty of these lot inside and outside of the sect, regardless of what some old guy they share a clan name with does or says<br /> -<br /> <br /> Gangrel are certainly capable of being just as rich and influential as their peers. There are many creative uses for animals.<br /> <br /> To a neonate, and some ancilla, it doesn't matter about high or low, because the divide is mostly forgotten and nonexistent in the modern Camarilla. An elder who was around for the dark ages may still think in that format, see traces of it in perception and treatment and add it to their list of grudges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-17-2021, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T03:12:24-07:00","id":1457015,"title":"","content":"Yes, I really don't see <b>how</b> the Gangrel could leave the Camarilla. Even if Xavier had a lot of clan prestige, I can't see anyone who felt they had an OK thing going deciding to declare themselves non-Camarilla on his say-so. Vampires in general are selfish,and Gangrel are more independent than most. it was a big blow to the Camarilla and Ventrue prestige, so I'd expect them to just tell Xaviar &quot;Don't let the door hit you on the way out&quot;, and pick some other Gangrel who stayed and had respect in the clan &quot;You are Justicar now&quot;<br /> <br /> The Gangrel who left I'd expect to be Gangrel who were not doing well in the cities, or almost Autarkis anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T07:08:34-07:00","id":1457023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457009#post1457009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plot dump - &quot;Xavier's met an antideluvian, but nobody believes him so now the clan is out.&quot;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me<br /> Only a minority of players give a fuck about the canonical characters. Hardestardt, Theo Bell? Ruddi? Vykos? Becket!? Masquerade really excels at setting, but the individual actors? Even if we put it nicely, these actors are Completely secondary to our own characters and our own cities. Unless you're like, Augustus Giovanni or Ur-Shulgi, who are more events than characters, few people want to see some bumblefuck in the limelight and making earth shattering, unwarranted, sweeping changes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T07:16:00-07:00","id":1457024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457023#post1457023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're like, Augustus Giovanni or Ur-Shulgi, who are more events than characters, few people want to see some bumblefuck in the limelight and making earth shattering, unwarranted, sweeping changes</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta hard agree with that. I love VtM and the metaplot and everything but I don't really give a fuck about the NPCs outside of handful of major ones who are, as you said, more like plot events than actual characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T08:22:22-07:00","id":1457026,"title":"","content":"One thing I always thought was interesting in the High/Low Clan divide is the question of the rights, obligations and preferences each has, and the differences between them. I imagined a separation akin to noble and merchant classes at the (european medieval) time. Like a Low would have to offer access to a Heaven or Herd he/she/it has if a High asks in a moment of need, or that if a Low insults a High, the one insulted has the right to defend its honor (and put the Low to death). Things like that.<br /> Besides that, there is the construct of clan unity some Clans like to promote, I assume the Ventrue, Toreador &amp; Tremere triumvirate like to do it best. That is why they are more worried about the actions of each member of their own clan, and coax and mold them to act accordingly, all the while trying to make other clan individuals look bad to pain an encompassing image of a Clan of freaks, barbarians, crooks or monsters. That way, when a X clan dude does something, they can all use it as an excuse to charge and tax that Clan more.<br /> <br /> As such, I see that when Xavier acts like a &quot;hey I'm crazy, I am seeing things that don't exist and all your vision is wrong about it, and you're all idiots by not seeing it too&quot;, maybe then the other Clans just used it as an excuse to grind and press more favors, troops and resources from the Gangrel. &quot;You gotta make reparations for the slide and insane allegations of Xaviar that made you all look bad&quot; would probably be a common speech. So, the Ven-Tor-Mere trio (and others of course) could've have squish every last drop they could from Gangrels deliberately, or weighted their hand way too much. So, more by the actions of other Clans over the Gangrel than the Clan itself, they felt &quot;fuck, this ain't worth it&quot; and were moving out, tired of getting the shaft. There is even a chance most Gangrel don't like to be thrown in the bucket of a Clan, where you got to act and respond as a representative from your clan. As such, when they are pressed for &quot;reparations&quot; of some sort, they get sick and tired of Camarilla worldviews.<br /> <br /> In summary, maybe Cam used Xaviar's scandal as a grievous outrage against them, and used it as an excuse to clutch and submit the Gangrel Clan even further, and to them this was the last drop of a long series of many small and some eventual (and big) problems they had with the sect. So they left. They were being treated as a medieval Low Clan again, that was inherently owing obligation and forgiveness to the all-mighty High Clans, so yeah, better go Anarch. I believe this would give more context to the Gangrel exodus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T10:12:36-07:00","id":1457033,"title":"","content":"Except for the antediluvians and &quot;antediluvians&quot;, like Tremere and Augustus, the NPCs are like the sample characters in the back of the clan books. Great for ideas, but I'll make my own stuff, thanks. Every one of my games set in the British Isles would ask &quot;Who the<i> fuck</i> is Mithras?&quot; Never heard of him. I've found that every non-American I've seen talk about this stuff disregards everything written about their home city/country anyway. I imagine some Americans also ignore the by Night books about their homes, too.<br /> <br /> Xavier? No such person. The Gangrel just do whatever and the Cam has 13 clans, even if four of them have special contracts that they only signed to humour the Ivory Tower, the Ravnos' placements are always either vacant or about to be, and by mutual agreement the Tzimisce typically don't attend social functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-17-2021, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T10:41:00-07:00","id":1457036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457026#post1457026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In summary, maybe Cam used Xaviar's scandal as a grievous outrage against them, and used it as an excuse to clutch and submit the Gangrel Clan even further, and to them this was the last drop of a long series of many small and some eventual (and big) problems they had with the sect. So they left. They were being treated as a medieval Low Clan again, that was inherently owing obligation and forgiveness to the all-mighty High Clans, so yeah, better go Anarch. I believe this would give more context to the Gangrel exodus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always my thought, that Xavier's hissyfit was just the tipping point, or the spark that lit the fuse. I don't see him (or Karsh, or Milov Patrenkov if still undead) having enough influence over the entire clan to declare secession by fiat, but without an active justicar the Gangrel may have found themselves getting the butt end of deals and political conflicts more than usual. Eventually such trends might be seen as more trouble than membership in the Camarilla was worth, and more and more individual vampires pack up and leave for greener pastures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T10:45:11-07:00","id":1457037,"title":"","content":"The High/Low clan concept only works as a mild prejudice. There are too many instances where you absolutely don't want to make it an institution. <br /> <br /> The Nos are the most powerful clan in the city, or at least you think they are. <br /> An 800 year old Gangrel may show up at any time to check on his childer. <br /> A posh Gangrel, a peasant-like Ventrue. <br /> Your rival gains a massive advantage from dealing with the low clans, one that could topple your rule, but you don't have a solid enough grasp to ruin him without a better pretense. <br /> <br /> ..and so on and so forth. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T11:40:35-07:00","id":1457040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457008#post1457008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel really aren't that bad at making money and building up territory (with animals) . They can ghoul and accumulate resources just the same as any other vampire. They do benefit from being able to take territory other vampires would struggle in. The Stereotype of poor, peniless Gangrel really only works for the very young or the vampires that actively eschew wealth for... whatever reason. (I suppose if your luck hates you and you get a facial animal feature, that can knock you down a bit, but you can still acquire great resources through ghouls and other proxies)<br /> <br /> The Low Clan/High Clan divide is just a bit of prejudice. Actively building a sect around it is just short-sighted lunacy. The worst you could do is not invite the low clans to parties, or give them bad seating arrangements. if you wanted to go further with it the &quot;high clans&quot; would eventually face the possibility of a slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Gangrel are only good at gaining wealth and power in a vacuum, since they aren't just competing with humans, they are competing with other vampires. They lack Presence and Dominate, and because of this they need to work on Attributes and Skills that compliment their actual Discipline spread. Meaning they will typically spend much of their younger years developing Stealth, Alertness, Survival, Brawl. By the time they are old enough to even think about anything other than survival, they have already spent huge amounts of time mastering the skills of a feral monster, and largely neglecting Social Attributes, and money/politics related Skills. Then you throw in their Clan Compulsion and Bane, which hurts their social interaction more than the High Clan's does their's.<br /> <br /> Sure, an individual Gangrel might be able to overcome all of those hurdles and become an economic/political powerhouse, but he/she is facing a huge uphill climb. And the few who do will be pretty much alone if the local High Clans close ranks to push him/her out of economic/political power. Something they can do as easily as declaring a certain economic/political area to be the Domain of the Toreador/Ventrue/Tremere Primogen. You managed to push that Ventrue out of the solar panel business? Too bad he's got the ear of the Prince, and the Prince says that solar panels are an extension of energy industry, and the energy industry is the Domain of that Ventrue, meaning you have no right to intrude on it, regardless of your business skill.<br /> <br /> Basically it's a lot of little things adding up over time that keeps the Low Clans as Low Clans. Discipline spreads, the mundane Attributes and Skills needed when young to compliment those Discipline spreads, socially crippling clan banes/compulsions, and finally the old boys club preventing remarkable individual exceptions from making much progress.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T12:04:51-07:00","id":1457041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457033#post1457033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the antediluvians and &quot;antediluvians&quot;, like Tremere and Augustus, the NPCs are like the sample characters in the back of the clan books. Great for ideas, but I'll make my own stuff, thanks. Every one of my games set in the British Isles would ask &quot;Who the<i> fuck</i> is Mithras?&quot; Never heard of him. I've found that every non-American I've seen talk about this stuff disregards everything written about their home city/country anyway. I imagine some Americans also ignore the by Night books about their homes, too.<br /> <br /> Xavier? No such person. The Gangrel just do whatever and the Cam has 13 clans, even if four of them have special contracts that they only signed to humour the Ivory Tower, the Ravnos' placements are always either vacant or about to be, and by mutual agreement the Tzimisce typically don't attend social functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lord knows I've done this. Do you know how lame my Boston campaign would be if I had to use the canon NPCs? A Malk Prince who thinks he's King Arthur? Fuck me sideways with a 4x4!<br /> <br /> I think literally the only thing I kept from the whole New England by Night material was that the Sabbat have a stronghold in Salem... and I used the NPC pack from Chaos Factor for its members because no one is going to interacting with them except to burn them to death anyway.<br /> <br /> I think the only named Vampires I've even used in ANY campaign were Shaitan and Tremere (in Goratrix's body) and those were in separate Mage campaigns and Aliea? and Ferrox from Gehenna in that one particular scenario. I MIGHT use Netchurch at some point, but only because there's a dhampir in the party and discovering his little horror show might be a fun side-plot (after which Netchurch will probably be a grease stain in my campaign world because my players don't give two fucks about respecting canon and the guy is a monster... the last thing going through his head is likely to be the Dhampir's Fist of God merit).<br /> <br /> About the only NPC I've ever managed to even remotely be interested in is Beckett, but only because he's basically a walking exposition machine used to lore dump all the actually interesting stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T12:13:37-07:00","id":1457042,"title":"","content":"Is taking what you want from VtM and chucking the rest a new thing? It seems weird for me to read this after seeing all the metaplot or census books made over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T12:58:37-07:00","id":1457045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457042#post1457042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is taking what you want from VtM and chucking the rest a new thing? It seems weird for me to read this after seeing all the metaplot or census books made over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally try to keep my setting as close to books as possible, with a few extrapolations or &quot;corrections&quot; to keep things smooth and consistent or more in line with reality; nothing radical.<br /> But that's from core books and the suplements that are purely setting/mechanics; The Thaumaturgy companions, Midnight seige, Hunters Hunted II, clanbooks.<br /> City books and chronicle books don't appeal to me, and I imagine they don't appeal to a lot of people. Now while there are name drops in something like Hunters Hunted II or clanbooks, there's nothing in these things that really endears me to a character like, say, a chronicle would, as chronicles spend a lot more time around a limited number of characters. I might have the vague idea to use Gratiano or Mithras, again &quot;event&quot; guys, if I ever set a game in their cities, but I'd run these fellows how I'd think they'd be, I wouldn't read up some roleplaying hints and closely follow his stat block.<br /> <br /> Maybe some people have a great attachment to, say, Rudi after helping him in his possibly good chronicle, but his summary sounds kinda stupid to me, so I'd ignore him. I played a longrunning game with a player who really liked the story of Jonas Albrecht, but again, I'd rather work with my own characters, and don't think this Jonas SNPC fellow matches the tone I take with the Garou/Silver fangs and I don't really like SNPCs having king-level sway in the plot. Just feels like someone got a bit self indulgent. The Margrave works better because he doesn't sound like someone's self indulgence. Characters like Jonas or Rudi or whoever just sound like someone got carried away with their own games and thought they should impose it on everyone else. That's why it's very easy to dismiss them.<br /> <br /> The best vampire example of someone who changes things in modern nights is of course, Ur-Motherfucking-Shulgi. Because he's not an SNPC, and the ST has plenty of leeway with how they want to work him.<br /> 1: His background is mysterious and the storyteller can make their own mystery adventure surrounding him. One storyteller's interpretation can differ wildly from anothers, but they can both be correct.<br /> 2. The Assamite schism was really something with a lot of buildup that needed an inciting incident. The Assamite sect was wonderfully fluffed with conflict. It's like WW1; If Franz didn't get Ferdinan'd, that war would've kicked off anyway because dreadnaughts and nationalism and Alsace-Lorraine and... stuff. Meanwhile the Gangrel... There's no good pretext.<br /> 3:It gave players more options with Assamites, not less. It's a win for both Cam and Anarch players because schismatics give them new character options (both welcoming and hostile), Loyalists get to double down and hunt traitors. It's a win for people who want to play religious assamites, Path of Blood fanatics and secular moderates, and it's also interesting for characters who hate assamites but now face them trying to intergrate.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel leaving the Cam is just... Loss.<br /> Someone had an opinion and now a lot of Gangrel with Cushy Cam possitions are jeapardized? Uh? No thanks. The Cam loses something. The Anarchs and Sabbat don't gain anything. The Gangrel lose something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T14:25:57-07:00","id":1457050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457042#post1457042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is taking what you want from VtM and chucking the rest a new thing? It seems weird for me to read this after seeing all the metaplot or census books made over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also do my best to stick with the spirit of the lore presented in the books, and incorporate metaplot developments.<br /> But frankly I'm playing this to have fun and sometimes the lore gets in the way, because it strikes me as uninteresting or in need of doctoring. I don't care about the premade NPCs and don't want them interfering with my story and character ideas. Sometimes I don't like a metaplot development. Caine and endgame Gehenna can fuck right off. Sometimes editions contradict each other and need reconciling. Sometimes I hate an entire spinoff and have to rehaul the whole damn thing starting with the mangling of languages in use.<br /> <br /> I've heard that many VtM players often tend to be very orthodox with lore, but I've always had the same group so it's never been a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-17-2021, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T14:43:52-07:00","id":1457052,"title":"","content":"In case I'm giving the wrong impression, I don't see any problem with treating metaplot and npcs like a salad bar. My biggest reason for preferring Requiem over Masquerade was that there wasn't (at least until 2E) really much of a metaplot, outside of New Orleans or Chicago. <br /> <br /> I'm just surprised because I thought the metaplot of WoD seemed to be the biggest selling point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T14:48:49-07:00","id":1457053,"title":"","content":"Requiem's toolbox approach and the total mystery of the setting is great. The appeal of Masquerade in comparison is indeed the lore (to me), but sometimes there's fun in filling in the blanks or reshaping that lore into what you want it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-17-2021, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T15:02:18-07:00","id":1457055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457053#post1457053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem's toolbox approach and the total mystery of the setting is great. The appeal of Masquerade in comparison is indeed the lore (to me), but sometimes there's fun in filling in the blanks or reshaping that lore into what you want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I always change things at least a little bit. As far as the Gangrel go, I basically assumed that Xaviar did leave just like the books said he did, but that many Gangrel ignored him and kept doing their own thing. (Of course, we started playing with V20 so this was all background material for my group anyway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T15:42:22-07:00","id":1457056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457052#post1457052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case I'm giving the wrong impression, I don't see any problem with treating metaplot and npcs like a salad bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that unreliable narrators are the order of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T18:19:54-07:00","id":1457066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457042#post1457042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is taking what you want from VtM and chucking the rest a new thing? It seems weird for me to read this after seeing all the metaplot or census books made over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal take is that if the PC's aren't the most central characters in my campaign, there's a problem with my campaign. This is their story and so everything in the campaign should be in service to their story. If that means some canon NPC gets the shaft or doesn't even exist because it would be disruptive, so be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T23:45:28-07:00","id":1457081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457033#post1457033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the antediluvians and &quot;antediluvians&quot;, like Tremere and Augustus, the NPCs are like the sample characters in the back of the clan books. Great for ideas, but I'll make my own stuff, thanks. Every one of my games set in the British Isles would ask &quot;Who the<i> fuck</i> is Mithras?&quot; Never heard of him. I've found that every non-American I've seen talk about this stuff disregards everything written about their home city/country anyway. I imagine some Americans also ignore the by Night books about their homes, too.<br /> <br /> Xavier? No such person. The Gangrel just do whatever and the Cam has 13 clans, even if four of them have special contracts that they only signed to humour the Ivory Tower, the Ravnos' placements are always either vacant or about to be, and by mutual agreement the Tzimisce typically don't attend social functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd lucky.<br /> <br /> None of my players would ever tolerate me going off-script in terms of setting lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T01:12:51-07:00","id":1457086,"title":"","content":"Never used it met a named NPC as far asi can recall, but then our games tend to be set fairly locally and rarely go world hoping as we play up the difficulty of a vampire just popping to another city for the weekend.<br /> Thinking of running Fall off London, in which case we'll use all the NPCs involved because that's what that chronicle demands, although I'll probably still change things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T02:01:25-07:00","id":1457089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457081#post1457081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd lucky.<br /> <br /> None of my players would ever tolerate me going off-script in terms of setting lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick is to have a group of casual players with no investment in the lore. New players help, just add a disclaimer that you're changing things a little from the text so they won't be confused if they go to someone else's game.<br /> <br /> The lore-orthodoxy of the fans is also why I've never tried to join another group, honestly. (Aside from not needing to)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-18-2021, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T02:35:50-07:00","id":1457090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457081#post1457081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd lucky.<br /> <br /> None of my players would ever tolerate me going off-script in terms of setting lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>My group is okay with it as long as I'm upfront about what I'll be changing and why I'm doing it. Sometimes I'll get a bit of pushback if a player really likes some bit of lore that I want to change, but in that case I'll usually try to find a way to keep it around if the player feels so strongly about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T11:02:52-07:00","id":1457114,"title":"","content":"Gangrel are most likely to be lore-orthodoxists, so when Camarilla changed something, they moved out XD <br /> JK","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T12:15:33-07:00","id":1457124,"title":"","content":"The Assamite schismatics don't really work as replacements. <br /> <br /> The appeal of the 7 was that they were really very broad-concept clans, except for the Tremere, who are really considered a subsect but also, from a magic perspective, embody the one magic philosophy that's very inclusive and encompassing (hermeticism) . The other six clans have very lose archetypes that for the most part can broadly work with a lot of people. Collectively the OG 7 cover every kind of person you might want to be as a vampire, while the clans outside of the Cam lend themselves more to very specific concepts and aren't that widely applicable. The Assamites aren't generalists like the vampires they've replaced. They have tons of baggage, their own caste system which hyper-focuses their character concepts, and are a mess with religion which doesn't really match the Secular nature of the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T12:36:33-07:00","id":1457128,"title":"","content":"There was no need for any replacements. There was no reason for the Gangrel or the Brujah to leave (not every Brujah is enraged by the establishment, sometimes they<i> like</i> the establishment. Their clan curse is being homicidally pissed off at things they don't like, not being cursed to defy the Camarilla).<br /> Also, nothing to replace them <i>with.</i><br /> <br /> All four independents are religious sects. The Western Ravnos are cut off from the spirituality of the clan, and the Family don't look it at first glance, but they're all religious cults and don't really fit neatly in the Camarilla (not to mention that two of them have a &quot;kill those who don't convert&quot; clause). The best you're getting is a &quot;we can do business so long as you don't cause shit in our domain and at least pretend to acknowledge our authority&quot; treaty, like the Promise, and apostates like the Assamite schismatics. Meanwhile the Camarilla <i>already had Lasombra</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T12:45:15-07:00","id":1457130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457128#post1457128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no need for any replacements. There was no reason for the Gangrel or the Brujah to leave (not every Brujah is enraged by the establishment, sometimes they<i> like</i> the establishment. Their clan curse is being homicidally pissed off at things they don't like, not being cursed to defy the Camarilla).<br /> Also, nothing to replace them <i>with.</i><br /> <br /> All four independents are religious sects. The Western Ravnos are cut off from the spirituality of the clan, and the Family don't look it at first glance, but they're all religious cults and don't really fit neatly in the Camarilla (not to mention that two of them have a &quot;kill those who don't convert&quot; clause). The best you're getting is a &quot;we can do business so long as you don't cause shit in our domain and at least pretend to acknowledge our authority&quot; treaty, like the Promise, and apostates like the Assamite schismatics. Meanwhile the Camarilla <i>already had Lasombra</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like complaining about the Assamites joining is weird as the HUGE CHANGES about their nature happened 20 years ago. The Vizier Clan made the Assamites a lot less...Assamitey.<br /> <br /> But that ship sailed a long time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T12:50:08-07:00","id":1457132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457130#post1457130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like complaining about the Assamites joining is weird as the HUGE CHANGES about their nature happened 20 years ago. The Vizier Clan made the Assamites a lot less...Assamitey.<br /> <br /> But that ship sailed a long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not complaining about them joining, just about the idea that they joined to replace anyone when I'm of the opinion that nobody should have left to be replaced. Sorcerers aren't common enough to replace the Tremere (though the idea of Assamite sorcerers and Tremere both being stuck together in the Camarilla on pain of death has got to make Elysium hilariously tense). Assamite warriors and viziers do not have the disciplines to replace the Gangrel or Brujah. They're not replacements, they're just another clan in the repertoir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-18-2021, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T15:56:51-07:00","id":1457152,"title":"","content":"Don't think of it as exact replacements. But getting big chunks of the Assamite and Lasombra clans helps shore up an organization that just saw many of its martially inclined members decide to take a powder, and its occult specialists go from a well-oiled machine to a disordered mess of squabbling factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T16:10:42-07:00","id":1457154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457152#post1457152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't think of it as exact replacements. But getting big chunks of the Assamite and Lasombra clans helps shore up an organization that just saw many of its martially inclined members decide to take a powder, and its occult specialists go from a well-oiled machine to a disordered mess of squabbling factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the reasons I found the demands the Carmilla made of the Lasombra in 5th a bit silly. Apparantly following the defection of the two primary martial clans and the prolapse of the Tremere the Ivory tower really thought it's in a position to negotiate absurd demands with two martial clans with a side interest in the occult. I'm suprised the reply from the Lasombra was &quot;lol no, you're down to 4.5 clans, we'll come back when you're down to you and the Malkavians and we'll want to be price.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T18:19:50-07:00","id":1457165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457154#post1457154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one of the reasons I found the demands the Carmilla made of the Lasombra in 5th a bit silly. Apparantly following the defection of the two primary martial clans and the prolapse of the Tremere the Ivory tower really thought it's in a position to negotiate absurd demands with two martial clans with a side interest in the occult. I'm suprised the reply from the Lasombra was &quot;lol no, you're down to 4.5 clans, we'll come back when you're down to you and the Malkavians and we'll want to be price.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that the whole Camarilla that made that demand? I thought it was one city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T19:47:06-07:00","id":1457169,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it did sound like a way too steep a price for Lasombra to go yeah-okay. But what I suppose is that the Friends of the Night (all the names in the Clan, including the one for the clan, are pretty silly imo) not only had their heads cleared from being chopped (that is actually true already), but took this opportunity to Clean the Freaking House. Like, imagine having the opportunity, reason, backing from most of your clan (and the Camarilla), to snap away with any member from your clan that you thought was less than loyal and perfect, imagine the coercive power the Friends had when they started looking around for the less valuable members of their clan to pay the price. Seems to me it wasn't much of a sacrifice, but a hitting of two birds with one stone. Lasombra are way too pieces of shike to be so collaborative.<br /> Each Prince is making it's own demand to accept the Lasombra, but it seems it isn't that different from Kevin Jackson's. Besides all that &quot;may not occupy high stations in 50 years&quot; or whatever, the Lasombra will thrive hard in the sect. A friend of mine and me share the belief that most of the Clan joined Sabbat because it was a better deal for them, and stayed there because of it. I imagine the Founders demands for the Lasombra weren't easy on the first guys to destroy their Founder, so Sabbat it was.<br /> <br /> Just like that, I also imagine the Gangrel joined Cam because it was the least amount of trouble for the most amount of benefits. Free circulation, end of that High/Low Clan bullshit, being pampered instead of spitted upon for drinking animal blood instead of butchering humans, always a place to be hired as a merc, not being hassled as an Anarch or Sabbat, Elysiums to crash in between travels.... seems like a fine deal. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T01:11:57-07:00","id":1457192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tofana by L'Oreal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1456514#post1456514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does Absimiliard's Gehenna Rex count? But seriously, the Book of Nod does mention ghouls in the First City:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gehenna Rex? You mean a ghouled Dinosaur from the <i>Gehenna</i> book?<br /> <br /> <br /> I was excited at the mention of Ghouls in the <i>Book of Nod</i> but then I read the quote. &quot;Those-who-serve, the latter-day ghouls, were the next lowest rung&quot;...seriously, this is all? The way I imagine Ghouls of the 3rd Generation Founders...<br /> <br /> There might be a woman who is a Ghoul of Arikel, and she is one of her closest friends and confidantes. She does research and knowledge gathering on all sorts of trends that the mortal societies follow, and always tries to deduce just what it might mean for the Clan Toreador and the wider Vampire society. And she travels the world, establishing cults of Arikel among Vampires and Ghouls (strictly Toreador Vampires and their Ghouls)...which are not simple cults of pleasure and hedonism, but more like cults of sensation and all sorts of experiences. And appreciation of love and beauty and art, of course. And this Ghoul of Arikel is <i>so</i> beautiful and attractive, but not in an obvious way. More than simply her appearance - it is in the way she carries herself, speaks, and acts.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is a man who is a Ghoul of Ennoia. Started out as a great warrior during the dark ages of Europe, and attracted Ennoia\u2019s attention because of his valor and courage. Nowadays he does not do much fighting unless it is necessary. But in such circumstances, he is a great and terrible warrior. He focuses more on gathering secret knowledge about the wild areas of the world \u2013 be it about specific mystic and wonderful places, or about animals, both mundane and legendary. He also acts as a messenger and herald among the Gangrel Vampires and their Ghouls, with the overall direction of being a peacebringer for the Clan Gangrel.<br /> <br /> <br /> So they would be favored servants, advisors, and friends, exalted in their service. Dealing with Vampires regularly; not exactly as equals, but definitely not being subservient to Vampires. And they would have high Attributes (might just be above five, after all it is Vitae of 3<sup>rd</sup> Generation Vampires coursing in their veins), developed Disciplines, and perhaps some blessings and unique powers received from their particular Founder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T04:16:04-07:00","id":1457199,"title":"","content":"The price was the culling of Sabbat Lasombra elders, right?<br /> If so, maybe it had something to do with the antitribu - or rather, the &quot;real&quot; Clan Lasombra, who suddenly had a bunch of snivelling weaklings daring to call themselves Lasombra crawling out of the Sabbat begging for mercy when they found out they'd fucked up and been debasing themselves and undeservingly bragging about it for centuries. (Although I don't think the Sabbat Lasombra (y'know the <i>&quot;real&quot;</i> Lasombra) agree with that assesment of events.) So it was like; &quot;You get one chance to prove you deserve to exist instead of us ripping your spine out here and now, here's a list of powerful elders we want dead. Anyone who can kill one and prove they did it gets a chance of living. Maybe. We'll consider it, anyway.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-19-2021, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T05:21:28-07:00","id":1457204,"title":"","content":"I think the Lasombra deal was more<br /> &quot;I don't want Lasombra here. But if you kill yourselves maybe I'll give you a chance&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm convinced that the people who wrote V5 Lasombra really don't clan. I've gone over it in detail in other threads, and I've yet to see a convincing counterargument. The V5 Lasombra don't really shore up the Cam's lack of fighters because A: They're mechanically really weak in V5, and B: Modern weapons really put fighting power into the hands of the Malkavians and Nosferatu and their bombs or the many minions of the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> I used to think the Assamites joining the cam would be a big deal for the tremere. Later on I concluded that the Tremere aren't really that threatened by the Assamite sorcerers because the Assamite sorcerer caste is not only miniscule but also... really backwards. The Tremere have a great organization, great standardization, and have magic easily adaptable to any belief system. The Assamites have very little in the way of any of that. This is why the Tremere have more paths and rituals despite being a fraction of the Assamite's age. The Asssamite sorcerers aren't going to become more like the Tremere because, well, who wants another Tremere? The Warriors and Viziers don't want to see the Assamite sorcerers become powerful enough to not rely on them, and the sorcerers don't want have their beliefs and practices pushed aside by standardization.<br /> Now Anarch sorcerers? Those guys are a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Cam should really try to include all the Clans except the Tzmisce, the Ravnos, and of course the Baali. Caitiff persecution is also fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T07:16:22-07:00","id":1457211,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's because they were working up to getting rid of the Sabbat as a pc faction (and possibly the independents, too) but didn't want to chuck out the signature clans of those sects.<br /> <br /> Bonus mages and more members is good, nevertheless, there is more to the Gangrel and Brujah than combat.<br /> <br /> That said, it occurs to me that - collapse of the pyramid and the struggle to put it back together aside - the Tremere should be making a killing in V5. I'm pretty sure they already did a tidy buisness in security and cosmetics, with a rise of hunters utilising increasing surveilance (who are specifically looking for unchanging individuals who can't perform certain human behaviours, like eating) those rituals would be in even higher demand. Hell, I'd expect a conspiracy theory that this is evidence that the Tremere are the puppetmaster behind the &quot;Inquisition&quot;, Vienna was faked to make them look weakened and divert suspicion. After all, everybody knows the scum will prey on other clans to profit themselves... Not even proper vampires, they're a bunch of thieving witches... There's a <i>reason</i> they're called usurpers... Hmm..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T08:36:42-07:00","id":1457212,"title":"","content":"Alas, there's no &quot;Ward against humans&quot;.<br /> Though there are some mystifying/keep away rituals, they don't stop dedication.<br /> <br /> The Tremere split can work as a kind of visual disarmment: The Tremere are just too successful, and a lot of people would like to see them knocked down a peg. The different houses work great for getting chantries into cities that wouldn't accept normal Tremere. The Anarchs, Sabbat and also some of the new Camarilla cities with former sabbat members all have a house directly catered towards their region.<br /> The problem with this theory is that it's too transparent, and, well, there's also going to be some people who don't like Tremere and who want to play the other houses thinking they're opposed.<br /> Organically, there's not really much chance of the three new houses spawning from the Tremere in earnest. The Tremere are not only rather likeminded, they simply don't recruit people that would think house Carna a good idea in any sufficient number, but they're also interdependent. The pyramid protects and nurtures more than it oppresses them. This split timed at the moment that the Camarilla downsizes and the Sabbat fucks off? Not a coincidence.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not a coincidence, but given how V5's writing works (or doesn't) it wouldn't be a suprise if the split happened just because the Cam got quartered but they knew people would still want to play Tremere who have chantries even if the cam isn't viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-19-2021, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T15:39:33-07:00","id":1457232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457204#post1457204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Lasombra deal was more<br /> &quot;I don't want Lasombra here. But if you kill yourselves maybe I'll give you a chance&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm convinced that the people who wrote V5 Lasombra really don't clan. I've gone over it in detail in other threads, and I've yet to see a convincing counterargument. The V5 Lasombra don't really shore up the Cam's lack of fighters because A: They're mechanically really weak in V5, and B: Modern weapons really put fighting power into the hands of the Malkavians and Nosferatu and their bombs or the many minions of the Ventrue.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll defend of a lot of stuff about v5 or at least play devils advocate but I have no idea what they were thinking with the Lasombra, it's the just plain bad writting. Not in the least because Oblivion is a terrible discipline for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T06:38:44-07:00","id":1457261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1342413-why-did-gangrels-leave-the-camarilla-i-mean-really?p=1457204#post1457204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Lasombra deal was more<br /> &quot;I don't want Lasombra here. But if you kill yourselves maybe I'll give you a chance&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Kevin Jackson fucked up but he was only an Ancilla.<br /> <br /> Because the Lasombra nodded and heard, &quot;We have to kill a shitton of Sabbat Elders on our way out anyway, so you just want proof.&quot; Besides, his deal wasn't LASOMBRA Elders but SABBAT Elders.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"h